{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487755-divorcing-clans-from-geography-people","id":1487755,"title":"Divorcing clans from Geography/People","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-07-24T11:53:36-07:00","id":1487755,"title":"Divorcing clans from Geography/People","content":"The first seven clans in VTM were universal, making fun of class rather than race; they work whether you're in Birmingham, Brisbane, Benin, Beirut or Bushan. Western Ventrue have some Roman terms, but it's very easy for Ventrue elsewhere to go with -insert favourite local empire here- influence instead. The Tremere are a relatively modern clan (I would argue THE modern clan) and though they have clear european origin they are a globalist clan with a globalist agenda that's ready to take in the best from anywhere. <br /> <br /> The other six clans began as racist caricature, and although steps have been taken to move us away from the worst of this, the result is quite mixed. I've convinced myself the best thing to do is move further in the direction of culturally neutral. <br /> <br /> <br /> Small changers: <br /> The Followers of Set, Great stuff. A religion that appropriates itself across all cultures <i>works</i>. Egyptian myth works well as a common framework (It's myths are famous and the mythology is old) <br /> <br /> Giovanni, Incestuous families all across the globe... somehow makes them less incestuous, but vampires heading mortal dynasties fun trope and this strategy players and the ST Invent their own culturally-fitting family appropriate for the location. Given that they've become less &quot;Other&quot; they really aught to just joint the Camarilla and become a normal clan. <br /> <br /> Lasombra: They're pretty good by V20. A paranoid, aggressive clan that likes the sea and fears God. Could use more antitribu and perhaps de-emphasize the Latin America stuff a little more, though that's not entirely something to be excised. We'll not talk about later editions; I don't want to despair. <br /> <br /> <br /> Big changes. <br /> Assamites: Still too tied to the middle east. The Loyalist/Schismatic split works wonders in seperating &quot;bloodthirsty fanatic&quot; from real world religions, but there are still problems on both sides: The Loyalists are still bound to the middle east, the schismatics serve as refugee allegory and have a far-too optimistic, orientalist narrative to them. If we start with the Schismatics, they've left the loyalists for varying and sometimes incompatible reasons, and it's not going to be easy for them to assimilate into rightly fearful Anarch and Camarilla populations. If we discuss Loyalists, well, I would posit that the Assamite bloodline is really geared far more towards them: the caste system that encourages them to operate interdependently, the darkening that sets them apart from other Cainites, the poison discipline that encourages cruelty, the addiction to diableire, the infamy of it all: they're basically designed to be their own sect. But with such a cannibalistic, militaristic sect, is this likely their only separation? Of course not. In addition to the Assamites that went to Chorizan/The Sabbat, there should have been tens of Assamite cells deciding they don't need the mountain and going on to create their own secluded sects in the far flung regions of the world, setting up shop over towns and small cities, adopting new beliefs, producing brainwashed childer, and making forays into nearby cities. When they're finally located and retribution comes, it will still be hard to stamp them out. So long as one survives, they can rebuild: a persistent threat. After a few cycles, these sects are likely to lose touch with their Alamut origins and completely localize. <br /> Also like, Evil Martial Art Sects are a fun trope that work in any culture. (But if they're vampire hunters I guess they have strong antihero potential?) <br /> <br /> Ravnos: Probably the messiest transition: Gypsies aren't a group that shouldn't be touched, so WW went orientalist on India. As great as the Samsara path of paradox is and how fitting the -reality is an illusion- mindset works, I doubt Indians feel flattered by being given the Ravnos. The philosophical influence of India on the clan is great, at least the ideas on Fate and Illusion perfectly fit the clan and these ideas have been exported to other parts of the world. On the otherhand, the Caste system can die in a ditch: Historically clueless, sociologically and politically unreasonable. While it could be imagined that some parts of the world appreciate Ravnos more than others, especially areas in conflict which need mercenaries, they really are a bloodline pushed towards nomadic behaviours. They're tragic mirrors of most Gangrel: One tries to be humane in order to avoid getting cast out, the other can't help but get cast out and learns to avoid being humane. <i>Ravnos work anywhere, with any human culture. </i> <br /> <br /> Tzmisce: Kupala should just get retconned out of existence. The Tzmisce come in two flavours: We have Terrifying doctors that threaten the establishment with their transgressive art, and we have a backwards eastern european caricature that amounts to little more than a shitty country Ventrue. The former works anywhere, the latter belongs to the last century and needs to go. @ me <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Bloodlines are smaller, so, reasonably, they could be tied to specific places as a result of not having time to develop. But I think it's quite inevitable that successful bloodlines such as the Samedi will move well beyond their starting culture.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-24T12:59:44-07:00","id":1487766,"title":"","content":"Just stating, I don't think they should make a too big retcon to produce such changes unless specifically asked by the affected people. It may backfire. But I can no problem engage with the exercise of examining how it could have been, or where to go if things come to this.<br /> <br /> <b>Followers of Set</b>: agreed. I'd add that the prejudice against them is too overblown one you take out the Thulsa Doom vibes. I'd add then to the Camarilla with some frequency or as default.<br /> <br /> <b>Giovanni</b>: instead of Venice they should have their own presence within the Dark Umbra, making up for an &quot;ancestral manor&quot; without ties to any particular place, which would both help to globalize their idea and their actual disparate families while keeping the idea of it being an extended clan (small caps), which would more easily justify the practice being widespread and their studies in Necromancy.<br /> <br /> <b>Lasombra</b>: they really should explore the ties with deep waters more, maybe even take the whole Venice thing the <b>Giovanni</b> currently have with mysterious elders living beneath the waters. A full blown <i>Innsmouth</i>-style theme for havens and domains would be nice.<br /> <br /> <b>Assamite</b>: i actually think that their post-schism + <i>Lore of the Clans</i> take is already pretty good on its own. Sure, the whole refuge take is an obvious implication, although it isn't spelled out too frequently, but that could be corrected just by moving the schism to the past, maybe even ancient times. And while Alamut is still in the Middle East, currently it is more of an undisclosed desert location with no ties to any particular country or population, which I think works well. Better than that, only if they moved into the Near Umbra (which their V20 <b>Dur-An-Ki</b> depiction would even give some credence to).<br /> <br /> <b>Ravnos</b>: something could maybe be done with the actual Jati system instead of the castes. We could even have splits within the clan regarding what the British did with the castes, or something else regarding their relationship with the other clans within India. But yeah, in general this whole mess is in such a state that I fully think it is the case to just ask Indian authors to make a book on the subcontinent and let them run wild with it. I would personally in this case let them work and only touch the clan again after they're done. Otherwise it is really a simple premise to work with other cultures, but the real problem from the beginning was the whole relationship with gypsies.<br /> <br /> <b>Tzimisce</b>: I disagree that their particular take on &quot;country lords&quot; should be ditched. It isn't particularly hard to move to other cultures and really consider that the overall phenomenon of land-based lords isn't really that much of an Eastern Europe thing.<br /> <br /> <b>Bloodlines</b>: they're small and specific and I think it is ok for them to be culturally specific even when starting to move out of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-24T15:53:26-07:00","id":1487792,"title":"","content":"Interesting ideas Personally I've always enjoyed an opposite approach of making then more grounded in local cultures. expanding on clan bases rather than altering the core. For example I explored athenian brujah, Muslim lasombra and Mexican tzmisce. I also explored a minor divide in the ventrue clan between germanic and Latin factions.<br /> <br /> <br /> I've been playing around with a celtic ventrue sub faction with links to the anarchs for months. The idea is their opposition to the carmarilla is more built on territorial encroachment than ideological. Anarch ventrue always felt very bland.<br /> <br /> I must admit I'm curious how tremere magic would work once you detached them from the western magic traditions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 07-24-2022, 07:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-24T20:05:15-07:00","id":1487834,"title":"","content":"<b>Tremere:</b> They are the worst imo. I'd make them far older. Maybe make it so that House Tremere only became dominant in Europe after the inquisition. House Carna being a resurgence of old pagan traditions then.<br /> <br /> <b>Ministry: </b>Localized cults are great, I'd imagine them as a vanguard of sorts for the orthodox church of set. Ministers not affiliated with the Church work well anywhere. I agree with reducing the prejudice against them as well.<br /> <br /> <b>Hecata: </b>The Giovanni already have a family in basically every country, and it's easy to add more. Cappadocians are good for more local lineages.<br /> <br /> <b>Lasombra</b>: They are really fine, I'd just enphasize that the ties to religion is uniform, so they have members amongst both Christians and Muslims for example. They are a main ashrra clan after all.<br /> <br /> <b>Banu Haqim: </b>I think we just need more Banu Haqim who aren't from the middle east. Some groups of BH who aren't tied to the middle east would be great as well. Especially in Asia.<br /> <br /> <b>Ravnos &amp; Tzmisce </b>are great in their V5 incarnation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27145-setitefriend","name":"SetiteFriend","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27145_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"255"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-24T20:26:54-07:00","id":1487835,"title":"","content":"I love the Tzimisce when they're not the freaky evil for evil's sake clan. Not exactly a good look for Slavs.<br /> <br /> I appreciate the &quot;lord of the land clan&quot; is being spread out to new countries.<br /> <br /> I think they'd do well in non-European regions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-24T20:31:05-07:00","id":1487836,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SetiteFriend</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487755-divorcing-clans-from-geography-people?p=1487834#post1487834\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Tremere:</b> They are the worst imo. I'd make them far older. Maybe make it so that House Tremere only became dominant in Europe after the inquisition. House Carna being a resurgence of old pagan traditions then.</div> </div> </div> </div>The whole thing with the Tremere is that they're specifically a continuity nod to <i>Ars Magika</i>. Also, their take on magic is somewhat more modern than specifically European, as it really isn't all that similar to European traditions older than the tail end of the 19th century. So it is something that can be adapted.<br /> <br /> But sincerely, if we go after them in this exercise I would take then out completely. Magic is the kind of element that works well without being tied to a specific clan, and we have the BH Sorcerers anyway for that, whose magic has origins with similar advantages to that of the Setites: it's all over the place and the original form is a culture long dead that virtually anyone can claim ties to today.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-24T20:38:48-07:00","id":1487837,"title":"","content":"I've recently come to a conclusion about the <b>Ravnos</b>. I think the reason the clan exists was to give the Gangrel a rival for the wilderness. Full stop. That avoided the issue of the PC Gangrel simply leaving their coterie in the city to live in peace in the countryside. Or the Gangrel in general simply avoiding other Kindred by staying in the wilderness. The Ravnos was the monkeywrench to be thrown into that idea. Now the Gangrel simply couldn't live in peace by themselves. They had a competitor. That is all that is needed for their clan concept.<br /> <br /> The entire Gypsy thing was to make sure the Ravnos and Gangrel were to be enemies since originally the Gangrel were supposed to be protective of Gypsies. The Ravnos obviously violated that, putting these clans in opposition. But that can easily be replaced with any other story/justification, ideally something involving a dispute between the clan's antedeluvians that poisoned relations permanently. Even if individual members of either clan didn't want to react that way, they couldn't rely that it wouldn't become hostile when meeting a member of the other clan. So it is a self-perpetuating cycle. Something a little bit stronger than the Brujah-Ventrue rivalry, but not to the point it becomes impossible for a PC Ravnos to be in the same coterie as a PC Gangrel, or doom every encounter to always end in a fight.<br /> <br /> You can keep the idea of Ravnos as wanderers, solitary tricksters, and enemies of the Gangrel while ditching any required ties to the Gypsies or India. Those just become options for character concepts like they would be any other clan.<br /> <br /> Chimestry as a Discipline still needs a lot of work though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-24T20:57:13-07:00","id":1487839,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487755-divorcing-clans-from-geography-people?p=1487836#post1487836\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The whole thing with the Tremere is that they're specifically a continuity nod to <i>Ars Magika</i>. Also, their take on magic is somewhat more modern than specifically European, as it really isn't all that similar to European traditions older than the tail end of the 19th century. So it is something that can be adapted.<br /> <br /> But sincerely, if we go after them in this exercise I would take then out completely. Magic is the kind of element that works well without being tied to a specific clan, and we have the BH Sorcerers anyway for that, whose magic has origins with similar advantages to that of the Setites: it's all over the place and the original form is a culture long dead that virtually anyone can claim ties to today.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Tremere are also a bloodline who stole a Clan's power so they're not something that is meant to be as ancient and widespread as other clans.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-24T21:35:03-07:00","id":1487842,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487755-divorcing-clans-from-geography-people?p=1487839#post1487839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Tremere are also a bloodline who stole a Clan's power so they're not something that is meant to be as ancient and widespread as other clans.</div> </div> </div> </div>From a Doylist perspective they have always been a clan, and since we're discussing the clans as game elements instead of their specific lore (after all, their regional ties do make sense in their specific lore, that wouldn't make a lot of sense to discuss), this is a strictly Doylist question.<br /> <br /> The Tremere are a bloodline from the 11th century because they're meant to be a bloodline from the 11th century. Otherwise they could have toppled the Salubri at any previous time or just have been a clan all along. The reason their lore is what it is is to bring them from <i>Ars Magika</i>, period.<br /> <br /> Nothing else in their concept requires this. Following the legendary roots of Hermeticism they could be Egyptian in origin. They could be Persian Magi, they could have ties to any old &quot;magical&quot; practice. Magic is not a Medieval invention and the clan doesn't need to be Medieval in origin to absorb Medieval developments into itself. Even the concept of the Tremere Pyramid could work as an organization outside the clans, or as something within any other clan or the Camarilla as a whole.<br /> <br /> It could have any of a number of justifications for the clan to be older, newer or non-existent and still follow mostly the same themes and concepts in the modern nights. It isn't only because it is specifically House Tremere.<br /> <br /> And that's why I would personally drop them entirely if we are to change their origin. Being House Tremere is, at the end, its whole <i>raison d'\u00eatre</i>. Without it I think there are better means to explore the concept of the Vampire Magician than a magical clan.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-24T21:43:51-07:00","id":1487843,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487755-divorcing-clans-from-geography-people?p=1487842#post1487842\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From a Doylist perspective they have always been a clan, and since we're discussing the clans as game elements instead of their specific lore (after all, their regional ties do make sense in their specific lore, that wouldn't make a lot of sense to discuss), this is a strictly Doylist question.<br /> <br /> The Tremere are a bloodline from the 11th century because they're meant to be a bloodline from the 11th century. Otherwise they could have toppled the Salubri at any previous time or just have been a clan all along. The reason their lore is what it is is to bring them from <i>Ars Magika</i>, period.<br /> <br /> Nothing else in their concept requires this. Following the legendary roots of Hermeticism they could be Egyptian in origin. They could be Persian Magi, they could have ties to any old &quot;magical&quot; practice. Magic is not a Medieval invention and the clan doesn't need to be Medieval in origin to absorb Medieval developments into itself. Even the concept of the Tremere Pyramid could work as an organization outside the clans, or as something within any other clan or the Camarilla as a whole.<br /> <br /> It could have any of a number of justifications for the clan to be older, newer or non-existent and still follow mostly the same themes and concepts in the modern nights. It isn't only because it is specifically House Tremere.<br /> <br /> And that's why I would personally drop them entirely if we are to change their origin. Being House Tremere is, at the end, its whole <i>raison d'\u00eatre</i>. Without it I think there are better means to explore the concept of the Vampire Magician than a magical clan.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm just saying that if you wanted to make sure 12 Clans were 12 Clans everywhere, you could do one exception as the cannibalistic usurpers.<br /> <br /> But, ironically, I think that would mean the Salubri would still be around because there's no way the House could get ALL OF THEM everywhere.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-24T23:05:05-07:00","id":1487847,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487755-divorcing-clans-from-geography-people?p=1487843#post1487843\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm just saying that if you wanted to make sure 12 Clans were 12 Clans everywhere, you could do one exception as the cannibalistic usurpers.<br /> <br /> But, ironically, I think that would mean the Salubri would still be around because there's no way the House could get ALL OF THEM everywhere.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Salubri being completely gone is overall a stupid plot anyway, but that's besides the point.<br /> <br /> Stopping to think about it, the Salubri could actually be the basis for the 12th clan. Not only because of their lore, but because vampires with good intentions, regardless of being successful or not in upholding them, are also a generic enough trope for the main clans. It would need a lot of work and a whole new take on their Discipline (probably ditching Obeah entirely or making it into a Blood Magic Path or something to that effect), but it would be a nice foil to the main take on the other clans without necessarily making them default good guys.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-25T02:47:06-07:00","id":1487853,"title":"","content":"I once did some notes up for Healer Salubri that were able to survive in Africa, the Middle East, and Asia that the Tremere eventually had to realize that they were never going to be able to deal with for a &quot;Global Camarilla&quot; campaign I had. The rub being the Tremere discovered most of them gave absolutely no shits about the diablerie of Saulot and were powerful enough the Tremere had to make peace with.<br /> <br /> The interpretation I went with was admittedy much darker but not ditching the concept entirely. The idea of trying to make a Clan of Salubri that has the same basic concept but dark enough to fit with the other Clans as well as a game of personal horror.<br /> <br /> Here's my notes:<br /> <br /> * The Salubri Clan weakness remained being unable to feed from unwilling vessels. Unwilling being defined as those not entranced, involuntarily there, or otherwise resisting. They are masters of loophole abuse on this.<br /> * The Salubri Embrace doctors, morticians, hospice owners, religious leaders, and people involved in the medical trade.<br /> * Lots of people do die because of the Salubri influence but they try to minimize their &quot;vampire footprint.&quot;<br /> * They are heavily involved in the local blood trades and frequently pass off spikes in deaths as the result of disease outbreaks.<br /> * Salubri have their own Roads that have survived since the Dark Ages that basically amount to &quot;God said it was okay to feed on you&quot; and &quot;Feeding from the already dying and elderly is fine.&quot;<br /> * Some Salubri blood bond people they consider undesirable and keep herds that are left to lose ghouldom but not their devotion. These people are willing vessels they feed on over the course of years until death.<br /> * Other vampires consider Salubri less saints and more, &quot;Hospital feeders.&quot;<br /> * Local variants of the Salubri included Animalism and Presence to go with Obeah because these allow a lot more feeding alternatives.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-25T02:48:58-07:00","id":1487854,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487755-divorcing-clans-from-geography-people?p=1487837#post1487837\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've recently come to a conclusion about the <b>Ravnos</b>. I think the reason the clan exists was to give the Gangrel a rival for the wilderness. Full stop. That avoided the issue of the PC Gangrel simply leaving their coterie in the city to live in peace in the countryside. Or the Gangrel in general simply avoiding other Kindred by staying in the wilderness. The Ravnos was the monkeywrench to be thrown into that idea. Now the Gangrel simply couldn't live in peace by themselves. They had a competitor. That is all that is needed for their clan concept.<br /> <br /> The entire Gypsy thing was to make sure the Ravnos and Gangrel were to be enemies since originally the Gangrel were supposed to be protective of Gypsies. The Ravnos obviously violated that, putting these clans in opposition. But that can easily be replaced with any other story/justification, ideally something involving a dispute between the clan's antedeluvians that poisoned relations permanently. Even if individual members of either clan didn't want to react that way, they couldn't rely that it wouldn't become hostile when meeting a member of the other clan. So it is a self-perpetuating cycle. Something a little bit stronger than the Brujah-Ventrue rivalry, but not to the point it becomes impossible for a PC Ravnos to be in the same coterie as a PC Gangrel, or doom every encounter to always end in a fight.<br /> <br /> You can keep the idea of Ravnos as wanderers, solitary tricksters, and enemies of the Gangrel while ditching any required ties to the Gypsies or India. Those just become options for character concepts like they would be any other clan.<br /> <br /> Chimestry as a Discipline still needs a lot of work though.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> To be fair, the notion of the Ravnos as a clan of vagabonds does exist in <i>some</i> World of Darkess books. The idea was that this was a group of vampires who rebelled against authority not, in the manner of the Brujah, through some manner of principle, but merely through a selfish desire to have complete freedom. You get this portrayal of the clan in, for instance, the core rulebook of the first edition of <i>Vampire: the Dark Ages</i>. There is certainly space within vampire society for a group like this, with such a portrayal of the clan giving a bit of additional range for characters existing on the fringes of vampire society. <br /> <br /> Yet there is a problem with the Ravnos, which is that they can't seem to maintain a single concept from book to book. So, we started out with &quot;Gypsy vampires&quot;, then went briefly into &quot;vagabond vampires&quot;, then into &quot;Indian vampires&quot;, then into &quot;kind-of-maybe-Indian-vampires-but-not-always&quot;. The result was incoherent, with each subsequent book making the clan harder to work with, just due to the accumulated mass of contradictions.<br /> <br /> Symptomatic of the issues (and to an extent causitive of them) is how the Ravnos were treated in the clanbooks of the revised era. With the Assamites, one could see what happens when a single author with a relatively coherent vision was allowed to shape the notion of a clan. So Clayton Oliver trimmed most of the orientialism off the Assamites, created a focused notion of the clan of judges, and gave the Assamites a much needed depth. He introduced a lot of ideas to the clan, but these ideas were primarily to enrich and sharpen the focus of the clan. The end result is by no means perfect, and comes off, in some instances, as a work in progress, but does effectively deal with many of the problems of the clan's original incarnation.<br /> <br /> The work on the Ravnos in the same era goes the other way. The clanbook, and the clan's entry in the Libellus Sanguinus series, throws a whole series of ideas at the clan without any coherence or depth. So you get an eastern and western clan, two Paths of Paradox, neither of which are terribly well considered, and a whole range of jati with no great relation to each other. The text draws upon India, but only in a very superficial way, and the writer seems to forget that India and the Mediterranean are actually linked by Iran and Syria. The ideas pull away from each other in different directions, and the seeming cause is the belief that the Ravnos are an ethnic clan (albeit Indian rather than Roma at this point) and that it would be worse to stereotype than to merely say the Ravnos can be anything. No wonder that, after this treatment, the Ravnos were unceremoniously bumped off.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/317-james_willoughby","name":"James_Willoughby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar317_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-25T03:19:49-07:00","id":1487855,"title":"","content":"&gt;Brujah rule Russia<br /> &gt;Gangrel rule the &quot;outlands&quot;<br /> &gt;Toreador rule France <br /> &gt;Tremere rule Austria<br /> &gt;Ventrue rule Germany and UK<br /> <br /> I mean, if it's a trope, let's apply it evenly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27252-hades","name":"Hades","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-25T10:54:04-07:00","id":1487914,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>James_Willoughby</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487755-divorcing-clans-from-geography-people?p=1487854#post1487854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yet there is a problem with the Ravnos, which is that they can't seem to maintain a single concept from book to book. So, we started out with &quot;Gypsy vampires&quot;, then went briefly into &quot;vagabond vampires&quot;, then into &quot;Indian vampires&quot;, then into &quot;kind-of-maybe-Indian-vampires-but-not-always&quot;. The result was incoherent, with each subsequent book making the clan harder to work with, just due to the accumulated mass of contradictions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep, it is very inconsistent. The problem was that after it was realized that tying the Ravnos too strongly to Gypsies created various issues, they couldn't figure out what was to be its core concept. Everything they tried was a riff of the original. Going from Gypsies to vagabonds wasn't a stretch. Neither was Gypsies to India since they originated in the sub-continent. But those are two very different directions. <br /> <br /> Furthermore, by themselves, those concepts didn't seem to give enough for STs and PCs. Changing from Romani to some greater Indian ethnos just made the group these vampires pulled from bigger, but kept it tied to human ethnic groups which was the same mistake. Trying to develop that aspect by the Path of Paradox and incorporate philosophical aspects associated with Hinduism wasn't productive in my opinion. It might have sounded good in theory, but in practice didn't help players or STs. &quot;Vagabonds&quot; by itself didn't do much either, since the Gangrel were already the wanderers.<br /> <br /> There's nothing inherently wrong with &quot;vagabonds&quot; as a concept. However, I think it's stronger for the game to emphasize their rivalry, competition, and feud with the Gangrel. It's a bit meta, but honestly it's why I think the clan exists. That's the narrative device that should matter to the game developer and STs. Vagabonds are just one character type that can associated to that.<br /> <br /> I think it is OK if both Gangrel and Ravnos are seen as &quot;wanderers&quot;. Outside that aspect, the two do have obvious differences. Gangrel tend more to be survivalists, explorers, hunters, warrior scouts, and other hearty frontier types. Ravnos are more like tramps, drifters, vagrants, traders, and others who live among human communities but travel. Gangrel culture prizes members who can take care of themselves, and live off the land by using their physical attributes. Ravnos culture prizes people who can prosper and gain treasure, using their wits and social skills. A well traveled business consultant living mostly in hotels who dispenses advice and moves on to her next client would fit well with the Ravnos, but not with the Gangrel. So would people who are perpetual tourists, travelling entertainers (especially those that follow large crowds like carnies or Ren Fairs), or people who are in the RV culture. They could even be property developers who build small resorts and move on! In the Dark Ages setting, they could also be religious pilgrims, bandits, and merchants. <br /> <br /> Gangrel are more like outdoorsmen who try to live in balance with their environment. Ravnos are nomads who exploit and deplete the area's scarce resources before moving on.<br /> <br /> You can keep the links to the Romani. You can even keep the links to India by saying that after their feud, Ravnos headed east from Mesopotamia to the Indus while Gangrel headed north or west. But the main use of the clan by STs, in my opinion, should be to provide competition to the Gangrel over the scarce resources of the Outlands. Their different cultures and preferred solutions to problems means the clans don't cooperate well. The one prefers physical prowess and mastery of one's environment, while the other chooses social interaction and exploiting human communities. In theory, the two shouldn't conflict, but they always do. Whenever Ravnos enter an area, they just create too many problems for the Gangrel because they inevitably attract too much attention. Then they leave, and the Gangrel who remain in that area have to deal with the mess - whether that be riled Lupines, hunters searching an area, police investigations, people or animals leaving the area, etc. Then when things finally settle down, some other Ravnos might move in and start the cycle again.<br /> <br /> As long as you keep in mind that the clan is supposed to be the Gangrel's rival, I think you can keep expanding concepts while retaining the core idea for the clan that the game needs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-25T17:15:55-07:00","id":1487951,"title":"","content":"You raise pretty much my point:<br /> <br /> * Make the Ravnos wanderers and vagabonds--we already have the Gangrel.<br /> <br /> * Make the Ravnos Tricksters and Mind-Fuckers--we already have the Malkavians.<br /> <br /> Which basically leaves the Ravnos as Gambit and Sexy Dancing Girl.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-25T19:12:46-07:00","id":1487964,"title":"","content":"If you must, some tables ive rolled at had interesting Astrological interpretations of the clans.<br /> <br /> Original Seven more or less fit the 7 Classical Planets.<br /> <br /> Revised 13 align with the Houses of the Zodiac. Yes, there are 13 Houses.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25883-inspectorg","name":"InspectorG","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-25T21:26:30-07:00","id":1487974,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487755-divorcing-clans-from-geography-people?p=1487792#post1487792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Interesting ideas Personally I've always enjoyed an opposite approach of making then more grounded in local cultures. expanding on clan bases rather than altering the core. For example I explored athenian brujah, Muslim lasombra and Mexican tzmisce. I also explored a minor divide in the ventrue clan between germanic and Latin factions.<br /> <br /> <br /> I've been playing around with a celtic ventrue sub faction with links to the anarchs for months. The idea is their opposition to the carmarilla is more built on territorial encroachment than ideological. Anarch ventrue always felt very bland.<br /> <br /> I must admit I'm curious how tremere magic would work once you detached them from the western magic traditions.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the thing, a germanic Ventrue is still a Ventrue. A japanese &quot;Daimyo&quot; Ventrue is still a Ventrue. Just as a muslim Lasombra is still a Lasombra.<br /> <br /> Individuals change based on their cultures; the clan however does not. A muslim Ventrue could be a Vizier, Caliph or Sultan, while a japanese Ventrue could be called a &quot;Daimyo&quot; or &quot;Shogun&quot;, and those could be Shintoist lords - but they would be lords still. A japanese Brujah could be a &quot;commoner ninja&quot; that hates the Ventrue Daimyos, but he's a Brujah still.<br /> <br /> Those vampires would have vastly different cultures, but they would find that the blood in their dead veins is the same. A japanese Ventrue Daimyo would consider a venetian Ventrue &quot;Doge&quot; a barbarian &quot;gaijin&quot; regardless, but would at least recognize their common &quot;higher pedigree&quot; than a venetian Brujah rabbel just the same as a ninja Brujah peasant ronim bastard.<br /> <br /> A Lasombra muslim Iman would still think that a Lasombra Bishop is a dirty kafir dog, and the Lasombra Bishop still thinks his Iman counterpart is an infidel heretic, but they still view each other as equals, or at least as slighthly better than some italian/russian Toreador degenerates. And they may even merrily join in hating some gangrel pagans.<br /> <br /> And so it goes with all others. Cultures and individuals change according to place and circumstances, but the overall aspects of each claim remains.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-25T22:02:46-07:00","id":1487978,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SetiteFriend</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487755-divorcing-clans-from-geography-people?p=1487834#post1487834\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Tremere:</b> They are the worst imo. I'd make them far older. Maybe make it so that House Tremere only became dominant in Europe after the inquisition. House Carna being a resurgence of old pagan traditions then.</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps it would be interesting to make them older than the Order of Hermes, and to predate them. Egypt would be a good starting place, if one isnt afraid to collide them with the Setites. Carthage is another option - but then again, Brujah and Ventrue shenanigans. Other options would be Babylon of Greece. Their origin on Babylon would be greatly served from the terrible mesopotamic gods.<br /> <br /> Another great idea that it just occured to me is to have them being sprung out of the italian etruscans. The etruscans were a civilization of a bunch of city states, much like Greece itself, with Rome being just simply one of those, but like the Macedonians ended up conquering the greeks, so too did the romans conquered the remaining etruscans. The etruscans had the - wait for it - &quot;cult of the mages&quot;, who were divinator oracles that predicted the future by reading the entrails of animals; that cult survived throughout all of Rome, all the way up to the christianization of Rome, and is the ancestral foundation of the Order of Hermes kabbalism in real life that would form the basis of european middle ages mysticism.<br /> <br /> The etruscan Tremere could then actually be an offset of the Ventrue clan in ancient Italy, who started as a bloodline but eventually divorced itself from the blue bloods - and after that yeah, ok, they eat up Saulot and become a &quot;proper clan&quot;.<br /> <br /> This would also be great in order to create this &quot;frenemy&quot; relation between Ventrue and Tremere, with the former considering the latter as their &quot;rebel children&quot;.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, if the Tremere bloodline started in Greece, it could greatly benefit from the &quot;hellenization&quot; during Alexander the Great, spreading over Egypt, Persia and India.<br /> <br /> Or even better, maybe the Tremere starts over both Italy and Greece, thus expanding with both the conquests of Alexander and with the Roman expansion. With the silk route, they go all the way to China and from there to Japan; with the islamic expansions, they go from Africa to Indonesia, and with the european great navigations, they reach the Americas.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SetiteFriend</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487755-divorcing-clans-from-geography-people?p=1487834#post1487834\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Ministry: </b>Localized cults are great, I'd imagine them as a vanguard of sorts for the orthodox church of set. Ministers not affiliated with the Church work well anywhere. I agree with reducing the prejudice against them as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've never been very found of the &quot;church of Set&quot;, and Set being depicted as a serpent always bothered me, but alas... I do like the idea of &quot;corruptors&quot; thou.<br /> I would divorce the Setites from ancient Egypt thou. They could work as any sort of corruptors for any culture thou - subjects of the Yama kings, medieval satanists, rakshasas, or even prophets of the Jotuns for the nordics, etc.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SetiteFriend</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487755-divorcing-clans-from-geography-people?p=1487834#post1487834\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Hecata: </b>The Giovanni already have a family in basically every country, and it's easy to add more. Cappadocians are good for more local lineages.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even the italian name is meh for a global clan. Personally, I would love to see Indian &quot;Giovanni&quot;/Hecata who are devout priests of Kali, or ancient &quot;Anubites&quot;/&quot;Hadean&quot; ones and somesuch.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SetiteFriend</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487755-divorcing-clans-from-geography-people?p=1487834#post1487834\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Lasombra</b>: They are really fine, I'd just enphasize that the ties to religion is uniform, so they have members amongst both Christians and Muslims for example. They are a main ashrra clan after all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Absolutely. Lasombra Imans, Rabi, Monks. Imagine how awesome (and unholy) to have a &quot;Lasombra&quot; Buddhist monk, or a Lasombra Taoist Priest and similar.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SetiteFriend</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487755-divorcing-clans-from-geography-people?p=1487834#post1487834\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Banu Haqim: </b>I think we just need more Banu Haqim who aren't from the middle east. Some groups of BH who aren't tied to the middle east would be great as well. Especially in Asia.</div> </div> </div> </div>Banu Haquim would make great Samurai, Janissaries or Templars. Basically any group of religious/nationalistic zealots would be great.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SetiteFriend</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487755-divorcing-clans-from-geography-people?p=1487834#post1487834\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Ravnos &amp; Tzmisce </b>are great in their V5 incarnation.</div> </div> </div> </div>I dont quite agree, but ok.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-25T22:12:48-07:00","id":1487980,"title":"","content":"Is there really a reason you can't have two vagabond Clans? <br /> <br /> You have two &quot;blue blooded&quot; Clans with the Lasombra and Ventrue. There were enough necromancer Clans that someone thought they needed to be merged together. And of course, there's all the different flavors of blood sorcers.<br /> <br /> I guess I'm a little conflicted about the Ravnos. In spite of their baggage (and the implications it came with), I want to like them. Something about a wandering, devil may care rogue sounds good on paper at least. And I always liked the aesthetic, for better or worse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3201-father-enoch","name":"Father Enoch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3201_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-25T22:16:06-07:00","id":1487981,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487755-divorcing-clans-from-geography-people?p=1487842#post1487842\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From a Doylist perspective they have always been a clan, and since we're discussing the clans as game elements instead of their specific lore (after all, their regional ties do make sense in their specific lore, that wouldn't make a lot of sense to discuss), this is a strictly Doylist question.<br /> <br /> The Tremere are a bloodline from the 11th century because they're meant to be a bloodline from the 11th century. Otherwise they could have toppled the Salubri at any previous time or just have been a clan all along. The reason their lore is what it is is to bring them from <i>Ars Magika</i>, period.<br /> <br /> Nothing else in their concept requires this. Following the legendary roots of Hermeticism they could be Egyptian in origin. They could be Persian Magi, they could have ties to any old &amp;quot;magical&amp;quot; practice. Magic is not a Medieval invention and the clan doesn't need to be Medieval in origin to absorb Medieval developments into itself. Even the concept of the Tremere Pyramid could work as an organization outside the clans, or as something within any other clan or the Camarilla as a whole.<br /> <br /> It could have any of a number of justifications for the clan to be older, newer or non-existent and still follow mostly the same themes and concepts in the modern nights. It isn't only because it is specifically House Tremere.<br /> <br /> And that's why I would personally drop them entirely if we are to change their origin. Being House Tremere is, at the end, its whole <i>raison d'\u00eatre</i>. Without it I think there are better means to explore the concept of the Vampire Magician than a magical clan.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I liked that idea. Iike that A LOT.<br /> <br /> That's it, no more &quot;clan Tremere&quot; in my games.<br /> <br /> Instead, there is &quot;The Pyramid&quot;, which will be a secret society inside of cainite society, that works within the Camarilla and transcends clans; it's sort of a sect inside a sect, The Pyramid is a group inside the Camarilla much like the Black Hand is to the Sabbath, and they hand pick their members to join from all across the clans, among those with potential for magic; a sort of &quot;Inconnu&quot; inside the Camarilla (the Camarilla's Black Hand would fit better).<br /> <br /> And the &quot;Black Hand&quot; would be a sort of &quot;antitribu&quot; for &quot;The Pyramid&quot; but inside the Sabbath.<br /> <br /> That would also solve the many problems of having dozens of silly bloodlines with Blood Magic; instead, ANYONE can learn Blood Magic (as an off clan discipline), if they manage to join either The Pyramid or the Black Hand.<br /> <br /> I loved that idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-26T00:49:12-07:00","id":1487986,"title":"","content":"Um, honestly I've always liked the regional ties of the various clans. They give a strong imprint to the clan and justify their influence in certain places as well as their &quot;concept&quot; of the clan itself.<br /> And for some time now, if before there was a stereotype problem, the Clans are much more global.<br /> The Followers of Set now infiltrate every cult and religious sect, for example.<br /> The Assamites already have within them a vast differentiation of skills and abilities, they dominate the uncontested Ashirra which is also the main interlocutor with the Camarilla at the moment.<br /> <br /> Perhaps the most problematic are the Ravnos, whose ties to India have only shifted the problem, but in general I don't find it necessary to eliminate the Eurasian origin of vampires.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26315-querion","name":"Querion","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-26T01:02:48-07:00","id":1487987,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487755-divorcing-clans-from-geography-people?p=1487951#post1487951\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You raise pretty much my point:</div> </div> </div> </div></span></span></span><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487755-divorcing-clans-from-geography-people?p=1487951#post1487951\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">* Make the Ravnos wanderers and vagabonds--we already have the Gangrel.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">* Make the Ravnos Tricksters and Mind-Fuckers--we already have the Malkavians.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Which basically leaves the Ravnos as Gambit and Sexy Dancing Girl.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br /> The Ventrue have the Lasombra and your beloved Tzmisce</span></span></span><br /> The Assamite Viziers are virtually Toreador <br /> The Baali and the FoS are strongly divided by religious differences and the results of these religious differences and nothing else. <br /> Necromancers.... the whole bloodline.<br /> <br /> And I'd argue &quot;mind fuckers&quot; is a title you can give to anyone with Obfuscate or Dominate, perhaps pressence. Certain Thaumaturgy paths can do it too. I wouldn't really label Ravnos as particularly good at &quot;mind fucking&quot;. Reallly I think their approach is probably going to be the most borish: Do what you want, move on before you get caught. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487755-divorcing-clans-from-geography-people?p=1487842#post1487842\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Tremere are a bloodline from the 11th century because they're meant to be a bloodline from the 11th century. Otherwise they could have toppled the Salubri at any previous time or just have been a clan all along. The reason their lore is what it is is to bring them from <i>Ars Magika</i>, period.<br /> <br /> Nothing else in their concept requires this. Following the legendary roots of Hermeticism they could be Egyptian in origin. They could be Persian Magi, they could have ties to any old &quot;magical&quot; practice. Magic is not a Medieval invention and the clan doesn't need to be Medieval in origin to absorb Medieval developments into itself. Even the concept of the Tremere Pyramid could work as an organization outside the clans, or as something within any other clan or the Camarilla as a whole.<br /> <br /> It could have any of a number of justifications for the clan to be older, newer or non-existent and still follow mostly the same themes and concepts in the modern nights. It isn't only because it is specifically House Tremere.<br /> <br /> And that's why I would personally drop them entirely if we are to change their origin. Being House Tremere is, at the end, its whole <i>raison d'\u00eatre</i>. Without it I think there are better means to explore the concept of the Vampire Magician than a magical clan.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting tidbit: the Tremere being founded in the 11th century coincides with the rise of European universities and to a more nebulous extent, the rise of guilds in Europe. Both have a lot of influence over what it is to be Tremere: The Tremere were never the inventors of vampire thaumaturgy, they were just the first to build their entire organization around it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-26T02:16:15-07:00","id":1487989,"title":"","content":"For me, the difference between Gangrel and Ravnos is that the Gangrel are much more bestial and are generally loners. The Ravnos are very human and aren't loners, they're travelers and they tend to travel with groups of people. I'd probably drop Animalism from the Ravnos and give them Obsfucate in order to make a stronger, clear distinction between the two clans.<br /> <br /> Basically the Gangrel are in the wilderness because they like it there. The Ravnos are in the wilderness only for as long as it takes them to get to the next city or town. While the Ravnos do generally spend more time in the wilderness than vampires from most other clans, they only do that when they have to (because they're travelling through the wilderness to get from one populated settlement to another or because they need to hide out off the map for awhile) not because they prefer being the wilderness over being in cities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 07-26-2022, 10:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-26T07:50:31-07:00","id":1488028,"title":"","content":"One of the big problems with the Ravnos is that while their concept is clear: wanderer troublemakers, the game completely failed at giving the players any meaningful reason to be so. That's the center piece of the problem, because anything we try to do with them have to account for this.<br /> <br /> So, how do you justify a network of vagabonds without being obnoxious about it? And how to do it while making PCs viable?<br /> <br /> I'm entertaining the idea that instead of a Weakness that forces them into being troublemakers (which is obnoxious), it could be something that gives them a reason to be wanderers most of the time, like a search for something, and let the troublemaker thing be just a consequence of so many of them being wanderers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-26T09:26:07-07:00","id":1488037,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487755-divorcing-clans-from-geography-people?p=1488028#post1488028\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of the big problems with the Ravnos is that while their concept is clear: wanderer troublemakers, the game completely failed at giving the players any meaningful reason to be so. That's the center piece of the problem, because anything we try to do with them have to account for this.<br /> <br /> So, how do you justify a network of vagabonds without being obnoxious about it? And how to do it while making PCs viable?<br /> <br /> I'm entertaining the idea that instead of a Weakness that forces them into being troublemakers (which is obnoxious), it could be something that gives them a reason to be wanderers most of the time, like a search for something, and let the troublemaker thing be just a consequence of so many of them being wanderers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, before of V5 many of the clans cultures were just simply that, just a cultural thing, not something intrinsic. So the Ventrue were loyalty due to culture, the gangrel are primitivists due to culture and so, save a few exceptions (like nosfs).<br /> <br /> So, maybe what the Ravnos are is just simply a cultural trait too. Once upon a time, everybody hated the Ravnos, so they had no choice but being nomads.<br /> <br /> Because they're nomads, they create problems - any unanounced outsiders do. And because of that, they are hated. And because they are hated, they are nomads... you get the meaning.<br /> <br /> Granted, that's <i>probably</i> not the best clan for player characters, but I dont think every single clan and bloodline should be avaiable to play anyway.<br /> <br /> Also, because their nomadism is part of their culture, they mostly only embrace mortals who are already wanderers, thus perpetuating the &quot;tradition&quot;.<br /> <br /> Why are they hated thou? Because. Nobody can remember what started it, but it's a self fueling cicle of prejudice.<br /> <br /> <br /> There. Their concept is done.<br /> <br /> How to &quot;internationalize&quot; this concept?<br /> <br /> Well, the first Ravnos to ever reach any new place in the ancient world were always wanderers. Upon reaching a place with vampires that know not them, they are foreigners - thus hated. And in places that they could eventually have been the first cainite settlers, others to come would bring their prejudices with them too - thus they are still hated.<br /> <br /> And due to that, they have to adapt, living as wanderer mercenaries, which makes them be even more distrusted, since their only affiliations and loyalties are with the highest bidder.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-26T09:42:41-07:00","id":1488039,"title":"","content":"Very interesting thread. Now I am personally not a huge fan or &quot;scholar&quot; of the Ravnos but I thought that I should offer some suggestions for Disciplines and Weakness that might work to make the Ravnos into wanderers and manage to survive in that role as well. Distances in the weakness isn't something I've gone to any degree of reflection and are essentially only suggestions.<br /> <br /> <b>Disciplines</b>: Replaced Chimestry with Obfuscate. I'm always to cut back on some unique Disciplines and Obfuscate would probably help them more on an average night than Chimestry would.<br /> <br /> <b>Weakness</b>:Essentially a 180 degree version of the Tzimisce weakness. The Ravnos can't sleep within 5 miles of their last sleeping place the next night or start to temporary lose Willpower dots. And they can't sleep closer than 3 miles from a place they slept in the previous 30 nights without again losing temporary Willpower dots.<br /> <br /> And that sleeping in a new place will start to restore Willpower, just like for the Tzimisce.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-26T09:44:16-07:00","id":1488040,"title":"","content":"Animalism+Fortitude are the perfect disciplines for Gangrel and Ravnos, who make their unlife thriving in the areas other vampires wouldn't consider. Obfuscate simply doesn't suit the outskirts or wilderness living half as well as Fortitude: these areas are mostly too open, and Obfuscate has a range limit. <br /> <br /> <br /> The Gangrel weakness has them heavily punished for bad behaviour: Bad behaviour increases the likelihood of conflict, degeneration, and frenzies. This creates beastial features, which &quot;punish&quot; the Gangrel. While older gangrel can learn to accept this, Young Gangrel are heavily incentivised to be humane and moderate.<br /> <br /> For Ravnos, Bad behaviour is mandatory. They're guaranteed to get into conflict. They are virtually helpless. This attracts them to ideas like Fate, or that they must as vampires reject humanity and follow a more compatible path, and to resent those who can more easily adopt humanity. <br /> <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5826_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5826\" data-vbnamecard=\"5826\">monteparnas</a> <br /> How do Ravnos organize? Phones? Before the invention of phones? Animalism? Birds? <br /> Potentially, they could learn a little thaumaturgy and communicate with their sires.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-26T09:52:34-07:00","id":1488041,"title":"","content":"For a role Ravnos could fulfill, as a network of vagabonds, here's an idea:<br /> <br /> A role that's not taken could be that of a &quot;bard&quot; or &quot;mysterious mystic&quot;, keeper/seeker of legends. As Nosferatu gather information and trivia that they can tipically verify, Ravnos could instead trade on unverifiable stories.<br /> <br /> Vampire has a lot of ancient Lore, it has a lot of uncomprobable legends and archeology (Book of Nod being the most famous) that, in spite of everyone having every reason to doubt about their veracity, vampires seem to view as quite important. It's not unreasonable, after all vampirism it's rather enigmatic, and the moves of the Jyhad does date back to myth and legend<br /> <br /> They would gather ancient tales and legends that could be sold as mystical mystery secrets, complete with relics fit for a<a href=\"https://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/BazaarOfTheBizarre\" target=\"_blank\"> Bazaar of the Bizarre</a>. Unlike the Setites, they wouldn't make a religion out of the mystery. Much of it it's going to be wrong if not lies...but since Cainite society it's often tied with the misterious and/or mystical it may well be that there's a lot of truth to it, and nodists know that there's a market for it.<br /> <br /> That way they have something to &quot;offer&quot;, that incidentaly also implies they would have something to &quot;search&quot; as they wander. And since these things are often forbbiden by the local sect, well, unfortunately they will be called troublemakers and liars. Also may or may not be prone to enjoy enigmas, and play tricks, as that's very related with the tropes of the mystic and talespinner.<br /> <br /> And if we kick the Tremere out, but want a clan with &quot;ready to go&quot; Thaum, these Ravnos could take the mantle, after all, what's magic if not esoteric secrets?. And since they would gather these from all over the world, you wouldn't need them to have one single, culturaly bound, Paradigm","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 07-26-2022, 12:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-26T12:56:29-07:00","id":1488079,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487755-divorcing-clans-from-geography-people?p=1488041#post1488041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For a role Ravnos could fulfill, as a network of vagabonds, here's an idea:<br /> <br /> A role that's not taken could be that of a &quot;bard&quot; or &quot;mysterious mystic&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Hence why they were in a very shallow way conflated with Gypsies.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487755-divorcing-clans-from-geography-people?p=1488041#post1488041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vampire has a lot of ancient Lore, it has a lot of uncomprobable legends and archeology (Book of Nod being the most famous) that, in spite of everyone having every reason to doubt about their veracity, vampires seem to view as quite important. It's not unreasonable, after all vampirism it's rather enigmatic, and the moves of the Jyhad does date back to myth and legend<br /> <br /> They would gather ancient tales and legends that could be sold as mystical mystery secrets, complete with relics fit for a Bazaar of the Bizarre. Unlike the Setites, they wouldn't make a religion out of the mystery. Much of it it's going to be wrong if not lies...but since Cainite society it's often tied with the misterious and/or mystical it may well be that there's a lot of truth to it, and nodists know that there's a market for it.<br /> <br /> That way they have something to &quot;offer&quot;, that incidentaly also implies they would have something to &quot;search&quot; as they wander. And since these things are often forbbiden by the local sect, well, unfortunately they will be called troublemakers and liars. Also may or may not be prone to enjoy enigmas, and play tricks, as that's very related with the tropes of the mystic and talespinner.<br /> <br /> And if we kick the Tremere out, but want a clan with &quot;ready to go&quot; Thaum, these Ravnos could take the mantle, after all, what's magic if not esoteric secrets?. And since they would gather these from all over the world, you wouldn't need them to have one single, culturaly bound, Paradigm</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmmm... I like that. Yeah, they could indeed have the &quot;Goblin Markets&quot; such as there is in CoD, this would be an awesome idea. I think we are beggining to get somewhere here","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24689,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","user":"Kakost","date":". 07-26-2022, 04:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-26T13:13:05-07:00","id":1488084,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gurkhal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487755-divorcing-clans-from-geography-people?p=1488039#post1488039\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b>Weakness</b>:Essentially a 180 degree version of the Tzimisce weakness. The Ravnos can't sleep within 5 miles of their last sleeping place the next night or start to temporary lose Willpower dots. And they can't sleep closer than 3 miles from a place they slept in the previous 30 nights without again losing temporary Willpower dots.<br /> <br /> And that sleeping in a new place will start to restore Willpower, just like for the Tzimisce.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487755-divorcing-clans-from-geography-people?p=1488028#post1488028\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of the big problems with the Ravnos is that while their concept is clear: wanderer troublemakers, the game completely failed at giving the players any meaningful reason to be so. That's the center piece of the problem, because anything we try to do with them have to account for this.<br /> <br /> So, how do you justify a network of vagabonds without being obnoxious about it? And how to do it while making PCs viable?<br /> <br /> I'm entertaining the idea that instead of a Weakness that forces them into being troublemakers (which is obnoxious), it could be something that gives them a reason to be wanderers most of the time, like a search for something, and let the troublemaker thing be just a consequence of so many of them being wanderers.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with Monteparnas here. Having their weakness forcing them to be like that is subotimal; most clans behaviors arent due to their weaknesses per se - or at least it wasnt until V5 and their compulsions.<br /> <br /> I honestly dont know for sure what their weakness could be. Maybe in line with Aleph's idea, something like the Toreador, but rather than being fascination for beauty and art, being for exoterism? I dont know.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-26T14:00:25-07:00","id":1488090,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gurkhal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487755-divorcing-clans-from-geography-people?p=1488039#post1488039\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Weakness</b>:Essentially a 180 degree version of the Tzimisce weakness. The Ravnos can't sleep within 5 miles of their last sleeping place the next night or start to temporary lose Willpower dots. And they can't sleep closer than 3 miles from a place they slept in the previous 30 nights without again losing temporary Willpower dots.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, how long can a Ravos lay in Torpor before taking aggravated damage?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3201-father-enoch","name":"Father Enoch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3201_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-26T17:04:56-07:00","id":1488113,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487755-divorcing-clans-from-geography-people?p=1488037#post1488037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, before of V5 many of the clans cultures were just simply that, just a cultural thing, not something intrinsic. So the Ventrue were loyalty due to culture, the gangrel are primitivists due to culture and so, save a few exceptions (like nosfs).</div> </div> </div> </div>True to a degree, but their weakness usually has some relationship with their culture and, more importantly, their cultures make sense as social developments. They give their members something that helps to survive and find a niche within Kindred society. They also have some momentum, something that doesn't outright force members to be like the rest, but at least reward those who fit. The Ravnos have a culture of... not fitting? Not even trying? Squandering opportunities and burning bridges for giggles? For all of eternity?<br /> <br /> Gangrel are survivalists, and while they're loners most of the time, they usually know each other and have some means of contact. If you fit the bill of the clan, you'll adapt to your territory, hunt in the wild and be self-sufficient. If you fit the bill of the Ravnos as we have it until now, you'll be a pariah everywhere and end up with nothing to your name after centuries, because you leave everything every time. And why? How to get a good enough explanation (we do have explanations for clan cultures) for this and what good does it bring to the game outside a very specific trope with limited use? (Nomad Ravnos arrives, everyone expects petty problems, the newcomer delivers, the city get rid of the troublemaker)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487755-divorcing-clans-from-geography-people?p=1488040#post1488040\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5826_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5826\" data-vbnamecard=\"5826\">monteparnas</a><br /> How do Ravnos organize? Phones? Before the invention of phones? Animalism? Birds?<br /> Potentially, they could learn a little thaumaturgy and communicate with their sires.</div> </div> </div> </div>My first idea was for leaving messages being a more common thing than sending news, specially in the past. But instead of Hobo Code-style shenanigans, it could be through stories and even books. A member of the clan disguises and embellishes their messages as tall tales and stories the locals will likely repeat for a long time, maybe they leave behind cheap story books of mediocre quality, and those stories have hints other Ravnos are likely to get that it is a message of a clan mate.<br /> <br /> Of course, such messages are unreliable in accuracy as the reader may misinterpret some things, but that's not necessarily a bug. When a Ravnos arrives at a city, they look for the places and people most likely to still remember old local tales or something like that.<br /> <br /> This is still a forming idea, but basically I think they would have a system to leave messages more than to spread news, as they focus more on finding their own next roads than being quick to contact the others. Their original Discipline spread could help, Animalism lets them spread tales and information through animals, Fortitude let them leave messages in places that are hard to reach because they're dangerous, and Chimerstry may be used to leave or hide messages.<br /> <br /> But otherwise I think just using letters would have been enough for most of them in the past, and a common information to spread would be your next destination, so most members always have a rough idea of where at least a few others are at any given time. Some could have magic rituals and whatnot, but that wouldn't be the rule even if we alter them into a Blood Magic wielding clan.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487755-divorcing-clans-from-geography-people?p=1488041#post1488041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A role that's not taken could be that of a &quot;bard&quot; or &quot;mysterious mystic&quot;, keeper/seeker of legends. As Nosferatu gather information and trivia that they can tipically verify, Ravnos could instead trade on unverifiable stories.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's an interesting approach, although I also think they could trade in news among the Kindred, too.<br /> <br /> In the past travelers were an important source of information about the world, and the Ravnos could be the ones transporting news from one place to another, even letters and packages, depending on how much they could be trusted for this. And I do think that easing the &quot;untrustworthy&quot; aspect on them is necessary, anyway.<br /> <br /> So when a Ravnos arrive, it marks the arrival of news and stories from other Domains, the things that would hardly get out even today in Kindred society. They bring legends and mysteries, but also gossip and more up-to-date information on what's going around the world. It would be a prime opportunity for a devious member of the clan to fabricate stories for their own benefit, but would also be a niche for those who make a name for themselves as good on their words.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-26T18:50:49-07:00","id":1488121,"title":"","content":"Bah, the Ventrue are ROYALTY, not loyalty... My goodness, I really need to pay more attention when typing, it's getting really gross, sorry about that.<br /> <br /> Anyway... There's also the option to drop them alltogheter... Just saying...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24689,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","user":"Kakost","date":". 07-26-2022, 09:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-26T19:00:34-07:00","id":1488122,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487755-divorcing-clans-from-geography-people?p=1488113#post1488113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">True to a degree, but their weakness usually has some relationship with their culture and, more importantly, their cultures make sense as social developments. They give their members something that helps to survive and find a niche within Kindred society. They also have some momentum, something that doesn't outright force members to be like the rest, but at least reward those who fit. The Ravnos have a culture of... not fitting? Not even trying? Squandering opportunities and burning bridges for giggles? For all of eternity?<br /> <br /> Gangrel are survivalists, and while they're loners most of the time, they usually know each other and have some means of contact. If you fit the bill of the clan, you'll adapt to your territory, hunt in the wild and be self-sufficient. If you fit the bill of the Ravnos as we have it until now, you'll be a pariah everywhere and end up with nothing to your name after centuries, because you leave everything every time. And why? How to get a good enough explanation (we do have explanations for clan cultures) for this and what good does it bring to the game outside a very specific trope with limited use? (Nomad Ravnos arrives, everyone expects petty problems, the newcomer delivers, the city get rid of the troublemaker)<br /> <br /> <br /> My first idea was for leaving messages being a more common thing than sending news, specially in the past. But instead of Hobo Code-style shenanigans, it could be through stories and even books. A member of the clan disguises and embellishes their messages as tall tales and stories the locals will likely repeat for a long time, maybe they leave behind cheap story books of mediocre quality, and those stories have hints other Ravnos are likely to get that it is a message of a clan mate.<br /> <br /> Of course, such messages are unreliable in accuracy as the reader may misinterpret some things, but that's not necessarily a bug. When a Ravnos arrives at a city, they look for the places and people most likely to still remember old local tales or something like that.<br /> <br /> This is still a forming idea, but basically I think they would have a system to leave messages more than to spread news, as they focus more on finding their own next roads than being quick to contact the others. Their original Discipline spread could help, Animalism lets them spread tales and information through animals, Fortitude let them leave messages in places that are hard to reach because they're dangerous, and Chimerstry may be used to leave or hide messages.<br /> <br /> But otherwise I think just using letters would have been enough for most of them in the past, and a common information to spread would be your next destination, so most members always have a rough idea of where at least a few others are at any given time. Some could have magic rituals and whatnot, but that wouldn't be the rule even if we alter them into a Blood Magic wielding clan.<br /> <br /> <br /> That's an interesting approach, although I also think they could trade in news among the Kindred, too.<br /> <br /> In the past travelers were an important source of information about the world, and the Ravnos could be the ones transporting news from one place to another, even letters and packages, depending on how much they could be trusted for this. And I do think that easing the &amp;quot;untrustworthy&amp;quot; aspect on them is necessary, anyway.<br /> <br /> So when a Ravnos arrive, it marks the arrival of news and stories from other Domains, the things that would hardly get out even today in Kindred society. They bring legends and mysteries, but also gossip and more up-to-date information on what's going around the world. It would be a prime opportunity for a devious member of the clan to fabricate stories for their own benefit, but would also be a niche for those who make a name for themselves as good on their words.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, those are interesting ideas. And yes, to make them more manageable rather than just &quot;KILL THE RAVNOS!&quot;, I agree on toneing down the trust issues.<br /> <br /> But then, why do they move? What compels them to be nomads?<br /> <br /> Because depending on the answers, it could change them from being hated to being a nuisance or being valuable assets to either Camarilla and/or Sabbath (Anarchs, whatever)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-26T19:36:05-07:00","id":1488126,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487755-divorcing-clans-from-geography-people?p=1488084#post1488084\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree with Monteparnas here. Having their weakness forcing them to be like that is subotimal; most clans behaviors arent due to their weaknesses per se - or at least it wasnt until V5 and their compulsions.<br /> <br /> I honestly dont know for sure what their weakness could be. Maybe in line with Aleph's idea, something like the Toreador, but rather than being fascination for beauty and art, being for exoterism? I dont know.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem seemed to be for a way to make the Ravnos wanderers. I proposed a solution by means of their weakness. Simple as that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Father Enoch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487755-divorcing-clans-from-geography-people?p=1488090#post1488090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So, how long can a Ravos lay in Torpor before taking aggravated damage?</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty much any amount of time. Lying in torpor is one long sleep for the most part. Now if the Ravnos would rise from torpor they would need to relocate or wake up the next time with no willpower points available. But if they keep sleeping uninterrupted, then they can stay in a single location for as long as they want/need.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":970,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","user":"Gurkhal","date":". 07-26-2022, 10:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-26T21:12:22-07:00","id":1488129,"title":"","content":"&quot;can't sleep within 5 miles of where they slept last night&quot; is a dumb weakness. They're probably just going to bounce between two locations. It's inconvenient, but it's not defining. It's anecdotal and boring. <br /> <br /> &quot;You have a vice that's difficult to supress&quot; is a phenomenally fun weakness. From a personal horror angle, from a psychological standpoint, from a sociological standpoint, from an economics standpoint... you're interesting. Hell, from this weakness alone, nevermind the other disciplines or the clan culture, this makes the Ravnos head and shoulders above most other clans on the scale of being intriguing. You are <i>bound </i>to commit a certain sin whilst in a state where you have to look after your humanity or switch to a Path. That's the state of being double-damned right there. Malkavians are half as interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-27T01:13:24-07:00","id":1488141,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487755-divorcing-clans-from-geography-people?p=1488129#post1488129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;can't sleep within 5 miles of where they slept last night&quot; is a dumb weakness. They're probably just going to bounce between two locations. It's inconvenient, but it's not defining. It's anecdotal and boring.<br /> <br /> &quot;You have a vice that's difficult to supress&quot; is a phenomenally fun weakness. From a personal horror angle, from a psychological standpoint, from a sociological standpoint, from an economics standpoint... you're interesting. Hell, from this weakness alone, nevermind the other disciplines or the clan culture, this makes the Ravnos head and shoulders above most other clans on the scale of being intriguing. You are <i>bound </i>to commit a certain sin whilst in a state where you have to look after your humanity or switch to a Path. That's the state of being double-damned right there. Malkavians are half as interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Please read the full weakness before commenting. Its no more dumb than the other weaknesses. And its specifically made to encourage/enforce a moving life style for the Ravnos.<br /> <br /> The only thing I see with the Ravnos weakness, posted below the comment to my suggestion, is a massive &quot;You're entitled to behave like an asshole with you character because its your weakness&quot; which places it firmly right next to fishmalk in its potential and use by certain players.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-27T03:19:31-07:00","id":1488151,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Father Enoch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487755-divorcing-clans-from-geography-people?p=1488090#post1488090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So, how long can a Ravnos lay in Torpor before taking aggravated damage?</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yeah...The developers surely didn't cover all their bases when they made this new clan flaw up...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2582-gangrel44","name":"Gangrel44","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-27T04:40:36-07:00","id":1488156,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gurkhal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487755-divorcing-clans-from-geography-people?p=1488141#post1488141\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only thing I see with the Ravnos weakness, posted below the comment to my suggestion, is a massive &quot;You're entitled to behave like an asshole with you character because its your weakness&quot; which places it firmly right next to fishmalk in its potential and use by certain players.</div> </div> </div> </div>A lot of weaknesses can let the player act like an asshole. Ventrue are my favourite. <br /> &quot;My feeding type is amputees, put your finger here.&quot; <br /> &quot;Damn it Clyde! Pure blooded Africans only, not Afro-American, not Afro-Carribean, We're not on a budget here: I eat Africans&quot;<br /> <br /> Lasombra are pretty great too<br /> &quot;My lack of reflection, I think he saw me, bring him&quot; <br /> <br /> The rules don't encourage fishmalks. Ravnos... ok, yeah, they can pick an annoying vice. But you're playing VTM not DnD: If a coterie member is very troublesome you're expected to get them killed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-27T06:42:46-07:00","id":1488163,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gurkhal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487755-divorcing-clans-from-geography-people?p=1488039#post1488039\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Weakness</b>:Essentially a 180 degree version of the Tzimisce weakness. The Ravnos can't sleep within 5 miles of their last sleeping place the next night or start to temporary lose Willpower dots. And they can't sleep closer than 3 miles from a place they slept in the previous 30 nights without again losing temporary Willpower dots.</div> </div> </div> </div>That feels like it could be a bit disruptive, especially for games that aren't set in the modern setting. Every night the Ravnos could end up taking several hours to join up with the rest of the player characters in town, and then need to leave an hour or two early so that they can get to somewhere they can sleep before the sun comes up. It's less of an issue in the modern setting, especially with cars and such.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-27T06:51:03-07:00","id":1488164,"title":"","content":"It could be a compulsion to explore. Ravnos could have a compulsive curiosity. Just like Toreador inevitably ends up bored with their playthings and needs a new object of their attention from time to time, so too a Ravnos could end up bored with the same old places, and feels compelled to get some new air.<br /> <br /> This would turn them into nomads, and even more than that, would make them the most cosmopolitan of the clans; Ravnos would become more than mere vagabonds with nothing to their names except a collection of narrow escapes from blood hunts, they would be explorers, mercenaries, traders and maybe even embassadors/pirates from distant lands, particularly before the industrial revolution","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-27T07:22:53-07:00","id":1488168,"title":"","content":"If I had to come up with a new Clan flaw for the Ravnos, I would probably make them a literal trouble magnet. Maybe the longer they stay somewhere, the more trickster spirits, asshole banes, Spooks, Haunters, whathaveyou gather around them and mess with <i>everybody</i>. Maybe they are catalysts for Bad Karma backlash that hits at the worst time. Maybe the Prince's favorite Faberg\u00e9 Egg gets spontaneously sucked into Oblivion. Either way, it starts with the Ravnos coming to town and leaves together with them. Have their flaw out-trickster them and ruin it for them even if they try to play nice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-27T07:37:11-07:00","id":1488169,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gurkhal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487755-divorcing-clans-from-geography-people?p=1488126#post1488126\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem seemed to be for a way to make the Ravnos wanderers. I proposed a solution by means of their weakness. Simple as that.</div> </div> </div> </div>V5 already does something like that. It is better than the usual, but more bookkeeping and inconvenient than encouraging for distinct play, and it has the disadvantage that it may make the long term presence of a Ravnos in the game too hard, which is the bigger problem.<br /> <br /> I think something that in general makes sense for them to be wanderers, but does not directly force it, better because then you can have exceptions that will work for a given game. As obligatory wanderers instead of just likely wanderers the Ravnos get too disruptive for most games, limiting their potential usage.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487755-divorcing-clans-from-geography-people?p=1488129#post1488129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;You have a vice that's difficult to supress&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Is an obnoxious weakness that may be extremely fun for your mental exercises, but causes the whole problem of pigeonholing them into the single trope of trouble-making Nuisance-of-the-Week vagabond that we can't do shit about their history and culture without stepping on the issue of them being obligatory assholes instead of only encouraged by this dark world to be assholes like the rest of the Kindred.<br /> <br /> You may not see any problem with this weakness, but I think a reasonable number of people here do and we'll keep discussing alternatives, thank you.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487755-divorcing-clans-from-geography-people?p=1488164#post1488164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It could be a compulsion to explore. Ravnos could have a compulsive curiosity.</div> </div> </div> </div>As long as that's put in such a way that they can live in the same place for decades exploring details and niches, I think it may work. I do want the possibility of a Ravnos staying for a reasonable amount of time to form connections and taking part in politics, as that both give us an easier time with PCs and increases the range of uses for them in the games. But then, most would be wanderers sooner than later, and <i>that</i> part would be a reasonably justified clan culture.<br /> <br /> Not necessarily the winner, but definitely pin that idea for later!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487755-divorcing-clans-from-geography-people?p=1488168#post1488168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I had to come up with a new Clan flaw for the Ravnos, I would probably make them a literal trouble magnet. Maybe the longer they stay somewhere, the more trickster spirits, asshole banes, Spooks, Haunters, whathaveyou gather around them and mess with <i>everybody</i>. Maybe they are catalysts for Bad Karma backlash that hits at the worst time. Maybe the Prince's favorite Faberg\u00e9 Egg gets spontaneously sucked into Oblivion. Either way, it starts with the Ravnos coming to town and leaves together with them. Have their flaw out-trickster them and ruin it for them even if they try to play nice.</div> </div> </div> </div>Better than the standard, but that may be too hard on the ST. Coming up with so many shenanigans for your game is a lot of work unless we have something to narrow down possibilities and make up for most of the work.<br /> <br /> In my opinion that works better in a crossover-friendly game, or at least with a crossover-capable ST, because then it is just a matter of intruding another gameline in the middle for the effect.<br /> <br /> As a baseline the Ravnos already have a stated problem with fae and Chimerstry spontaneously creates Chimera. That's an awesome source of problems that isn't too hard <u><b>when</b></u> you're well versed in Changeling. You can more or less easily change that to spirits or even specters, but the requisite of being well versed on another game remains. Without that, we would need a lot of work to make this usable without focusing too much of the ST's energy on the Ravnos.<br /> <br /> Pin that idea, but it needs a lot of work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-27T08:38:37-07:00","id":1488172,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487755-divorcing-clans-from-geography-people?p=1488169#post1488169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As long as that's put in such a way that they can live in the same place for decades exploring details and niches, I think it may work. I do want the possibility of a Ravnos staying for a reasonable amount of time to form connections and taking part in politics, as that both give us an easier time with PCs and increases the range of uses for them in the games. But then, most would be wanderers sooner than later, and <i>that</i> part would be a reasonably justified clan culture.<br /> <br /> Not necessarily the winner, but definitely pin that idea for later!</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, it could be that they can stay in the same place for decades, but once in a while they just need a &quot;weekend off&quot; to &quot;recharge the batteries&quot;. So, every once in a while they have an urge to travel somewhere new. This gets worse for elders, because while neonates can explore neighborhoods of their own hometown they never went in before, the longer you live the smaller the world gets... So after exploring all neighborhoods of your town, you'll have to explore neighbor towns; after that, neighbor states. And so it goes, always searching for somewhere new.<br /> <br /> This could have all sorts of impacts - first, elders have a harder time, and the older the Ravnos, the more prone to becoming a full nomad.<br /> <br /> On the other hand thou, going into torpor is a great way to &quot;refresh the scenery&quot; without leaving your home! <br /> <br /> Now, while this is a nuisance for them and even potentially dangerous, it also means they arent just a bunch of weirdos that every once in a while pop up out of nowhere, cause a ton of mayhem and disappear back again, as in the weird Doctor Who episode of the week.<br /> <br /> They could live in a fixed location, take permanent residence in a town where they'll have their power base, and engage in cutthroat backstabbing politics like all the other &quot;pretty&quot; clans.<br /> <br /> Their insatiable curiosity however is what gives them a fame of &quot;trouble makers&quot;; more often than not, you'll find a Ravnos sticking their noses where they dont belong, if you get my meaning. It's just irresistible to them, their curiosity is simply too great.<br /> <br /> This means they would make great spies and infiltrators, for instance.<br /> <br /> Also, a small inter clan culture that I believe could be a nice touch; you would have two main &quot;cultural zeitgeists&quot; within the clan, like you yourself already realized, some of the Ravnos would just simply &quot;live in the roads&quot;, and never stick on one place for long. Those would follow all the traditional rituals - present to the local Prince, enjoy their allowed time of welcoming, and taking off. Those travellers would do great for both/either Camarilla or Sabbath, bringing outside news.<br /> <br /> And the second time would be those that take permanent residence (althought having constant absences to explore close places for some periods of time).<br /> <br /> Now, those two groups need not be totally permanently distinct, as if two forever apart bloodlines. Instead, they can be fully interchangeable: some Ravnos spend a century or 2 in a single city, disappearing 1 week every month to explore around, but after those 2 centuries he takes off and spends 1 entire century wandering all over, until deciding to take residence in a new city on the other side of the globe for the next 50 years and so on.<br /> <br /> Also, another important aspect of Ravnos culture would become &quot;Claim of Hospitality&quot;; traveller Ravnos can most of the time count on being welcomed by other Ravnos that have permanent residency somewhere.<br /> <br /> This culture of the clan would also cause lots of political problems; imagine a Prince that has problems with overpopulation, but the local Ravnos keep insisting on allowing their clan members full hospitality.<br /> <br /> Also, cainites being naturally paranoid, it aint easy to deal with those annoying nomads always sticking their noses were they dont belong.<br /> <br /> So, I guess Curiosity could be an excellent Weakness/Compulsion for them, that would make the Ravnos far more interesting and part of the world rather than just the weird happenstance that annoys everybody once in a while.<br /> <br /> And, they would still be competition to the Gangrel.<br /> <br /> Just imagine the Ravnos &quot;clan's reunions&quot;, where they share stories of their travels and share among one another tales of exotic lands and incredible adventures.<br /> <br /> Ravnos would also be incredible bards due to that; I envision Toreador being fascinated by their storytelling skills, while nosfs are always all too eager to try to farm any useful informations among their stories, and Ventrue giving the grump face to those undisciplined rabble constantly bringing dynamism to their courts.<br /> <br /> I mean, I guess it's better than making them automatic trouble magnets that cant interact with the cainite society<br /> <br /> This could even create their own peculiar","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-27T09:08:39-07:00","id":1488175,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487755-divorcing-clans-from-geography-people?p=1488169#post1488169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">but causes the whole problem of pigeonholing them into the single trope of trouble-making Nuisance-of-the-Week vagabond that we can't do shit about their history and culture without stepping on the issue of them being obligatory assholes instead of only encouraged by this dark world to be assholes like the rest of the Kindred.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>But they aren't one note assholes, they're complex. Sure, Ravnos A is compelled to do one bad thing when a good opportunity presents itself. There's little to help that, but the important question is where do they go from there? Do they sequester themselves away, guiltily overcompensate, try to make up for their wrongs, do they accept their compulsion and not let it define them, or do they accept &quot;destiny&quot; and allow their vice to define them, as is done by those on the path of paradox? Having a shitty hand doesn't end the game for you. Does your vampire have to be an irredemable villain because he drinks blood? No. Does your Ravnos have to be a monster or liability to you coterie because he can't stop with the meth/gambling/seducing people already in a monogamous relationship? Not really. <br /> <br /> Also nuisance players can ruin any clan. If someone's going to make a shit character, it's the ST's job to veto; rewriting everything to minimise the damage an idiot player can do is a fools errand.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-27T09:22:13-07:00","id":1488176,"title":"","content":"The problem with the Ravnos is that their clan concept simply isn't a clan concept. It's more like a subset of anarch: the wandering grifter. OWOD was bad about putting sect-subset concepts into clans and V5 has inherited its mistake.<br /> <br /> In fact, it probably always should have been a common archetype for Gangrel childer. The deep forests are owned by werewolves and Gangrel elders. The deep city is owned by the High Clans. So some Gangrel dance around the edges being grifters while they slowly develop their powers enough to carve out a territory in the wilderness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3598,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","user":"CajunKhan","date":". 07-27-2022, 02:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-27T16:22:08-07:00","id":1488222,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487755-divorcing-clans-from-geography-people?p=1488176#post1488176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem with the Ravnos is that their clan concept simply isn't a clan concept. It's more like a subset of anarch: the wandering grifter. OWOD was bad about putting sect-subset concepts into clans and V5 has inherited its mistake.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Ravnos are also tailor made for the Anarchs but aside from, &quot;Yeah, there's some there&quot;, I don't think they were ever made a part of it.<br /> <br /> I would, however, simply stick with Ravnos can never sleep in the same place twice.<br /> <br /> Thus it's weird but not DISRUPTING. You can sleep in a different room of the same motel every night and that's annoying but it's not going to make you wonder how you stay in Chicago for your Chicago by Night game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-27T16:36:11-07:00","id":1488223,"title":"","content":"Sorry, responded to the wrong thread. Oops","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3201-father-enoch","name":"Father Enoch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3201_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-27T17:26:32-07:00","id":1488228,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487755-divorcing-clans-from-geography-people?p=1488175#post1488175\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But they aren't one note assholes, they're complex.</div> </div> </div> </div>Complex or not, they're obligatory assholes and no complexity changes the many limitations imposed by this, and the unavoidable pettiness of their brand of assholery. And there's a world of difference between &quot;you can make an effort to have a Ventrue with a particularly dark blood dependence&quot; and &quot;you must make a huge effort to come up with a vice that won't led your Ravnos to be expelled from the city in two weeks&quot;.<br /> <br /> As they are, they're so limited in use that I would easy exchange them by almost any bloodline and end up with a better option for a Great Clan.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-27T18:26:24-07:00","id":1488236,"title":"","content":"For my own games I changed the Ravnos flaw a bit and made it so that they are compelled by both a vice (something that causes trouble for other people) and a virtue (something that causes them to help other people). Ravnos dance between being devils and saints. They upset the status quo and cause trouble, whether by creating problems or looking to solve them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-27T19:42:13-07:00","id":1488240,"title":"","content":"Rather than compel the Ravnos to perform a crime or other action, I'd just make it easier for them to lose Humanity/Path ratings. A penalty to Conscience/Conviction rolls, not Self-Control. That is a weakness that is still associated with the idea that the Ravnos are morally weak or prone to sins, but doesn't take away agency or possibly lead PCs and STs into scenes that nobody at the table wants. It's also a legitimate penalty, as it'd be easier for Ravnos to lose themselves to the beast if they up their ante past petty crimes into serious violations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-28T00:33:25-07:00","id":1488247,"title":"","content":"There are a number of issues here with making this change. One is that Clan is both a political distinction and a mystical one. Must there be an Antediluvian for it to be a Clan or merely the vampiric lineage must be influential? It\u2019s both in the lore. The Tremere become a dominant vampire faction while they also usurp an existing Clan and diablerize the Antediluvian. This creates a problem with universalizing Clans. <br /> <br /> The recent usurpers, then, should remain bloodlines. It\u2019s too far fetched and certainly not culture neutral to have usurper Clans eliminate the usurped Clan nearly entirely. <br /> <br /> Tremere are a bloodline then, maybe a powerful and respected one, but a bloodline nonetheless and they are heavily focused in Europe and the West since they arose in Europe. The Giovanni could just be a faction of the Cappadocians, they don\u2019t even need to be a mechanically different bloodline. <br /> <br /> Ravnos should probably just be a bloodline of Gangrel. Making them the Indian Clan was exactly the wrong direction.<br /> <br /> Here is a heretical idea - Tzimisce as a Gangrel bloodline. The Gangrel are nature vampires, this leads to them being outsiders and removed from vampire politics. They won\u2019t be politicking in the city and they are out in the woods drinking deer blood. But the Tzimisce could be a bloodline that settled down as rulers of the land, making them a Clan of rulership but not politicians or city dwellers, but rulers who harken back to feudal lords who were tied to farms and forests. Ravnos are the nomadic Gangrel, while the Tzimisce are territorial. The Gangrel Clan itself is widespread, but the Tzimisce bloodline is often associated with Eastern Europe, the Ravnos are often associated with nomadic groups, including but not limited to Gypsies. <br /> <br /> The Setites are vampires who follow an evil deity and corrupt others. This could be universalized - make them the Baali Clan. The Setites are the Egyptian Baali who serve either Set or Apep, where as other Baali form different cultures could worship Christian style demons or any number of other manifestations of evil. <br /> <br /> The Lasombra are already detached from real world culture, they aren\u2019t the Mediterranean Clan. We can keep them the same. <br /> <br /> The Assamites became the Middle Eastern Clan just as the Ravnos became the Indian Clan. Both were bad ideas in my opinion. I don\u2019t know if Assamites can be universalized. What if we toss out the Assamites and put in the Salubri. The Salubri are a Clan of philosophers were peruse Golconda and have a strong distaste for the evil actions most vampires engage in. The warrior Salubri are conceptually melded with the Assamites, and have become known as vampire killers and many became corrupt diablerists. <br /> <br /> So, in this scenario we have these Clans:<br /> Brujah<br /> Toreador<br /> Malkavian<br /> Nosferatu<br /> Ventrue<br /> Lasombra<br /> Gangrel (Tzimisce and Ravnos are bloodlines)<br /> Baali (Setites as a bloodline)<br /> Salubri (Assamite concepts are filled by altered warrior Salubri)<br /> Cappadocian/Hecata (Giovanni are a bloodline or faction, don\u2019t make them usurpers)<br /> <br /> Tremere become a bloodline, not really tied to another Clan. <br /> <br /> This only leaves us with 10 Clans, but they are more universal culturally/geographically.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-28T04:10:37-07:00","id":1488251,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487755-divorcing-clans-from-geography-people?p=1488247#post1488247\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are a number of issues here with making this change. One is that Clan is both a political distinction and a mystical one. Must there be an Antediluvian for it to be a Clan or merely the vampiric lineage must be influential? It\u2019s both in the lore. The Tremere become a dominant vampire faction while they also usurp an existing Clan and diablerize the Antediluvian. This creates a problem with universalizing Clans. <br /> <br /> The recent usurpers, then, should remain bloodlines. It\u2019s too far fetched and certainly not culture neutral to have usurper Clans eliminate the usurped Clan nearly entirely. <br /> <br /> Tremere are a bloodline then, maybe a powerful and respected one, but a bloodline nonetheless and they are heavily focused in Europe and the West since they arose in Europe. The Giovanni could just be a faction of the Cappadocians, they don\u2019t even need to be a mechanically different bloodline. <br /> <br /> Ravnos should probably just be a bloodline of Gangrel. Making them the Indian Clan was exactly the wrong direction.<br /> <br /> Here is a heretical idea - Tzimisce as a Gangrel bloodline. The Gangrel are nature vampires, this leads to them being outsiders and removed from vampire politics. They won\u2019t be politicking in the city and they are out in the woods drinking deer blood. But the Tzimisce could be a bloodline that settled down as rulers of the land, making them a Clan of rulership but not politicians or city dwellers, but rulers who harken back to feudal lords who were tied to farms and forests. Ravnos are the nomadic Gangrel, while the Tzimisce are territorial. The Gangrel Clan itself is widespread, but the Tzimisce bloodline is often associated with Eastern Europe, the Ravnos are often associated with nomadic groups, including but not limited to Gypsies. <br /> <br /> The Setites are vampires who follow an evil deity and corrupt others. This could be universalized - make them the Baali Clan. The Setites are the Egyptian Baali who serve either Set or Apep, where as other Baali form different cultures could worship Christian style demons or any number of other manifestations of evil. <br /> <br /> The Lasombra are already detached from real world culture, they aren\u2019t the Mediterranean Clan. We can keep them the same. <br /> <br /> The Assamites became the Middle Eastern Clan just as the Ravnos became the Indian Clan. Both were bad ideas in my opinion. I don\u2019t know if Assamites can be universalized. What if we toss out the Assamites and put in the Salubri. The Salubri are a Clan of philosophers were peruse Golconda and have a strong distaste for the evil actions most vampires engage in. The warrior Salubri are conceptually melded with the Assamites, and have become known as vampire killers and many became corrupt diablerists. <br /> <br /> So, in this scenario we have these Clans:<br /> Brujah<br /> Toreador<br /> Malkavian<br /> Nosferatu<br /> Ventrue<br /> Lasombra<br /> Gangrel (Tzimisce and Ravnos are bloodlines)<br /> Baali (Setites as a bloodline)<br /> Salubri (Assamite concepts are filled by altered warrior Salubri)<br /> Cappadocian/Hecata (Giovanni are a bloodline or faction, don\u2019t make them usurpers)<br /> <br /> Tremere become a bloodline, not really tied to another Clan. <br /> <br /> This only leaves us with 10 Clans, but they are more universal culturally/geographically.</div> </div> </div> </div>I liked the ideas of making some of the clans as bloodlines.<br /> <br /> But, rather than have the Gangrel being the &quot;core&quot; clan with Ravnos and Tzi being branches, how about having all the 3 as equals? Thus being &quot;half clans&quot;. As if it were just a one single clan divided in 3, without any single one forming the &quot;core&quot;.<br /> <br /> That could also be based on the 3 life styles of each: Nomads for the Gangrel, Semi Nomads for Ravnos (with all the peculiars I brought in the previous page) and sedentary for the Tzis.<br /> <br /> As for the Tremere, I liked the idea of turning them into a secretive organization rather than a clan; that also has the benefit of curbing all the blood magic spread out everywhere nonsense, so now the Camarilla has &quot;The Pyramid&quot; and the Sabbath has the Black Hand as organizations that delve into Blood Magic, anybody can learn it thus if invited, and is not clan bound. Therefore, Blood Magic becomes more of a tool of elders.<br /> <br /> The Salubri are an incredible clan, their purge was a really bad idea. And someone suggested making the Osiris as a bloodline of theirs, I like that idea<br /> <br /> The &quot;Baali Clan&quot; is a good idea too. I never liked all too much all the &quot;religion of Set&quot; anyway, especially because the real life myth of Set is NOT a serpent, but an antropomorphized Chacal. So I always gave the ugly face to all the serpentis &quot;turning into a snake&quot; thing.<br /> <br /> Also, if the Setites are a thing, and other clans will even deal with them with &quot;just&quot; SOME prejudice instead of automatic blood hunt as with the Baali... What's really the difference?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-28T18:33:25-07:00","id":1488298,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487755-divorcing-clans-from-geography-people?p=1488251#post1488251\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I liked the ideas of making some of the clans as bloodlines.<br /> <br /> But, rather than have the Gangrel being the &amp;quot;core&amp;quot; clan with Ravnos and Tzi being branches, how about having all the 3 as equals? Thus being &amp;quot;half clans&amp;quot;. As if it were just a one single clan divided in 3, without any single one forming the &amp;quot;core&amp;quot;.<br /> <br /> That could also be based on the 3 life styles of each: Nomads for the Gangrel, Semi Nomads for Ravnos (with all the peculiars I brought in the previous page) and sedentary for the Tzis.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I like that idea too..<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487755-divorcing-clans-from-geography-people?p=1488251#post1488251\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The Salubri are an incredible clan, their purge was a really bad idea. And someone suggested making the Osiris as a bloodline of theirs, I like that idea<br /> <br /> The &amp;quot;Baali Clan&amp;quot; is a good idea too. I never liked all too much all the &amp;quot;religion of Set&amp;quot; anyway, especially because the real life myth of Set is NOT a serpent, but an antropomorphized Chacal. So I always gave the ugly face to all the serpentis &amp;quot;turning into a snake&amp;quot; thing.<br /> <br /> Also, if the Setites are a thing, and other clans will even deal with them with &amp;quot;just&amp;quot; SOME prejudice instead of automatic blood hunt as with the Baali... What's really the difference?</div> </div> </div> </div>That works. If the Children of Osiris are Salubri and the Setites are Baali, then it becomes a smaller part of the long war between the Salubri and Baali, which also includes Assamites who are now a faction of the Salubri.<br /> <br /> Another heretical possibility is folding the Lasombra into that Clan, since Obtenebration would make a great Discipline for a Clan dedicated to worshipping gods of darkness and/or demons especially with Abyssal Mysticism.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-29T00:24:01-07:00","id":1488331,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487755-divorcing-clans-from-geography-people?p=1488163#post1488163\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That feels like it could be a bit disruptive, especially for games that aren't set in the modern setting. Every night the Ravnos could end up taking several hours to join up with the rest of the player characters in town, and then need to leave an hour or two early so that they can get to somewhere they can sleep before the sun comes up. It's less of an issue in the modern setting, especially with cars and such.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487755-divorcing-clans-from-geography-people?p=1488169#post1488169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">V5 already does something like that. It is better than the usual, but more bookkeeping and inconvenient than encouraging for distinct play, and it has the disadvantage that it may make the long term presence of a Ravnos in the game too hard, which is the bigger problem.<br /> <br /> I think something that in general makes sense for them to be wanderers, but does not directly force it, better because then you can have exceptions that will work for a given game. As obligatory wanderers instead of just likely wanderers the Ravnos get too disruptive for most games, limiting their potential usage.</div> </div> </div> </div>As someone who is primarily interested in historical settings for Vampire I can readily understand the trouble that it would put on a Ravnos character. And I will readily agree and accept that my suggestion is more geared towards nomadic kind of games as opposed to more traditional ones.<br /> <br /> However I would also mention that I think that I wrote in my post that the exact distances are not set in stone or something I\u2019ve devoted a great deal of reflection. So if you want to make the distances shorter but keep the general idea of the weakness that would be perfectly ok with me.<br /> <br /> What I however find as an advantage with my suggestion over, for example, the \u201cCuriosity Weakness\u201d is that my weakness does not come with a motive which is forced into the character concept which in my humble view would steer the clan towards a stereotype.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-29T02:55:38-07:00","id":1488346,"title":"","content":"Perhaps it would do better to have more concrete rules for what constitutes a vice or not? (Malkavians could also benefit) or to have the vice only apply to mortals (much like how a Ventrue doesn't mind feeding from a supernatural that doesn't fit his feeding preference, the Ravnos feels no compulsion to enact his vice directly against other supernaturals)<br /> <br /> <br /> or perhaps the Vice only concerns itself with vampiric behaviour..<br /> Drug addiction (remember for Vampires this is a feeding issue) <br /> A compulsion to feed from a particular type of person (children, beautiful men, anyone who's visibly angry) <br /> Victimizing vessels before/after feeding. <br /> robbing/Taking trophies/ branding the vessel. <br /> Extreme territorial behaviour. <br /> Creating touchstones that they overzealously protect. <br /> Particularly malicious frenzies. <br /> Doesn't resist the Beast for certain frenzy conditions. (Insults, fire)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-29T05:22:58-07:00","id":1488354,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487755-divorcing-clans-from-geography-people?p=1488298#post1488298\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That works. If the Children of Osiris are Salubri and the Setites are Baali, then it becomes a smaller part of the long war between the Salubri and Baali, which also includes Assamites who are now a faction of the Salubri.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm... I liked that. That way, the Osiris/Setite conflict becomes just a localized in Egypt part of the more overall Baali x Salubri conflict<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487755-divorcing-clans-from-geography-people?p=1488298#post1488298\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another heretical possibility is folding the Lasombra into that Clan, since Obtenebration would make a great Discipline for a Clan dedicated to worshipping gods of darkness and/or demons especially with Abyssal Mysticism.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's VERY heretical lol.<br /> <br /> I actually like the Lasombra as an even WORSE conterpart of the Ventrue, and personally wouldnt want that gone. Also, that would be a focus only on their discipline, which by that metric could also apply to the Hecate/Cappadocians/Giovanni.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-01T10:37:15-07:00","id":1488723,"title":"","content":"I just took a few words in Latin to try to devise some cool names for the clans, at least for Europe, so that we would at least have have something better than &quot;Witch&quot; in modern spanish (Brujah) or french-like names such as &quot;Toreador&quot;, so that the clans can truly take their origins from ancient times. Here are a few options:<br /> <br /> Princeps - the first one (Ventrue)<br /> Venusta - Charm, beauty (Toreador)<br /> Vecors - Mad (Malkavian)<br /> Sylvaticus - Wild (Gangrel)<br /> Iracundus - Angry, Passionate (Brujah)<br /> Nosferafu (same) - this is a much more modern name based on fiction literature and movies, but it's freaking awesome, so I thought it would be nice to keep it.<br /> Tremere (same) - medieval clan, so no Latim name<br /> <br /> <br /> Now, I'll see what we get for the others, and after that, those would be the european versions of the clans; a chinese &quot;Princeps&quot; would still be the same clan, but would have their own name - yes, I'll search for something cool in mandarim in a while.<br /> <br /> Edit: so, our old Ventrues for example, could name themselves &quot;Princeps&quot; in Europe or &quot;Wangzi&quot; in China. That could potentially cause some confusion, but they would still share the same vampiric lineage, but with different cultural baggages","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24689,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","user":"Kakost","date":". 08-01-2022, 01:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-01T11:11:59-07:00","id":1488727,"title":"","content":"I think vampires are far more likely to use sobriquets and euphemisms to refer to the clans and bloodlines than they are to use formal names. Dignity has it's place, but the Masquerade is more demanding. You can discuss &quot;Blue bloods&quot; or &quot;lunatic&quot; in any context and it doesn't attract much interest and comes with a strong level of plausible deniability, &quot;Ventrue&quot; on the otherhand... well, obscure literature or videogames are probably going to be assumed, but there's a chance it doesn't get overlooked, and even a mild inquiry can undermine a vampire. I think there is a place to make very formal names from archaic languages, perhaps room to do it ironically, but for the most part it's going to be everyday -local language- for most vamps. <br /> <br /> <br /> Also the term Malkavian is <i>-perfect-</i> how dare you try to change that? <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-01T21:59:40-07:00","id":1488761,"title":"","content":"I have always had the thought that the Clan names that we know are just those used in modern English speaking countries. In other places and/or times the Clan names were/are different. For example, in Spanish speaking countries it\u2019s unlikely that Lasombra is called Lasombra, which would be like calling them Theshadow. I actually think that if any Clan is likely to Latinize their name, it\u2019s the Tremere. Historically, many scholars and noteworthy people latinized their names - Carolus Linnaeus, Christopher Columbus, Nicholas Copernicus. I wouldn\u2019t be surprised to see the Tremere as Tremereus. <br /> <br /> Back to the Lasombra - I do actually like the Clan as is, though I also think that Obtenebration would great a great Discipline for the Baali and/or Setite Clan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-01T22:36:28-07:00","id":1488763,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487755-divorcing-clans-from-geography-people?p=1488761#post1488761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> though I also think that Obtenebration would great a great Discipline for the Baali and/or Setite Clan.</div> </div> </div> </div>Baali? Probably.<br /> Settite? I don't think so. Yes, the snakes like darkness, but Obtenebration's abyss is really a sort of extreme realm that drives the fear of God/Devil into you. It encourages a severe gravitation towards a more strict monotheistic/duality kind of faith, rather than the &quot;anything goes&quot;/I'm a god too&quot; approach that Setites currently have. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-02T00:19:50-07:00","id":1488767,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487755-divorcing-clans-from-geography-people?p=1488723#post1488723\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just took a few words in Latin to try to devise some cool names for the clans, at least for Europe, so that we would at least have have something better than &quot;Witch&quot; in modern spanish (Brujah) or french-like names such as &quot;Toreador&quot;, so that the clans can truly take their origins from ancient times. Here are a few options:<br /> <br /> Princeps - the first one (Ventrue)<br /> Venusta - Charm, beauty (Toreador)<br /> Vecors - Mad (Malkavian)<br /> Sylvaticus - Wild (Gangrel)<br /> Iracundus - Angry, Passionate (Brujah)<br /> Nosferafu (same) - this is a much more modern name based on fiction literature and movies, but it's freaking awesome, so I thought it would be nice to keep it.<br /> Tremere (same) - medieval clan, so no Latim name<br /> <br /> <br /> Now, I'll see what we get for the others, and after that, those would be the european versions of the clans; a chinese &quot;Princeps&quot; would still be the same clan, but would have their own name - yes, I'll search for something cool in mandarim in a while.<br /> <br /> Edit: so, our old Ventrues for example, could name themselves &quot;Princeps&quot; in Europe or &quot;Wangzi&quot; in China. That could potentially cause some confusion, but they would still share the same vampiric lineage, but with different cultural baggages</div> </div> </div> </div>I have to disagree somewhat. By using Latin names, yes, we can push the origin of the names back one or two thousand years or so, but it don't make them the original names that the Clans would have used in their early history.<br /> <br /> EDITED: Besides I don't get the feeling that the Roman Empire was such a huge thing for the Cainites that it would have left a strong legacy like that.<br /> <br /> Secondly I would think that there would have developed certains terms used across mortal borders within the Kindred/Cainite subculture. Thus that there's a term of &quot;Lasombra&quot; for this Clan that has grown to become commonly used even while there may be local terms for local use as well. A Ventrue might use the term of Princeps, but for ease of commuication (s)he should also be familiar with the internationally accepted term &quot;Ventrue&quot; for her/his Clan..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-02T03:14:17-07:00","id":1488779,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487755-divorcing-clans-from-geography-people?p=1488761#post1488761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have always had the thought that the Clan names that we know are just those used in modern English speaking countries. In other places and/or times the Clan names were/are different. For example, in Spanish speaking countries it\u2019s unlikely that Lasombra is called Lasombra, which would be like calling them Theshadow. I actually think that if any Clan is likely to Latinize their name, it\u2019s the Tremere. Historically, many scholars and noteworthy people latinized their names - Carolus Linnaeus, Christopher Columbus, Nicholas Copernicus. I wouldn\u2019t be surprised to see the Tremere as Tremereus. <br /> <br /> Back to the Lasombra - I do actually like the Clan as is, though I also think that Obtenebration would great a great Discipline for the Baali and/or Setite Clan.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, Columbus was italian, who is a language close to latin. Only Linnaeus were swedish, but his surname already had a latinized origin from birth (the &quot;ae&quot; at the end is typically a latinized form), while his first name is Carl, wich is a Germanized version of a latin name and one of the most common names in Europe. In fact, it's the same name as mine in a different form - Carl in swedish; in portuguese, spanish, french and italian, Carlos (my name), Karl in german (my username) and in english it became Charles - so technically I also have the same first name as the prince of England, and Charles V of the HRE and Carlos Martel of France and many many others. The latinized form of which is &quot;Carolus&quot;. Linnaeu also adopted a french version after nobilization, &quot;Carl Von Lin\u00e9&quot;, a mix of French (the surname) and german (the &quot;Von&quot; title&quot;), from the time that French was the &quot;common tongue&quot; of Europe.<br /> <br /> Also, &quot;Christopher&quot; is the english form of the guy's name, his original name in italian was Cristoforo Colombo. In latim it was Christophorus Columbus. And &quot;Nicholas&quot; is also only the english form of Copernicus, and his name has a ton of variations for each language, one for english, german, french, spanish and portuguese. The original polish version of which was Miko\u0142aj Kopernik. In the case of Copernicus, it isnt that his name was &quot;latinized&quot;, but rather that it was &quot;italianized&quot;, his most popular name outside german or polish are variations of the italian variation, given the importance of the italian city states at the time. So, it isnt so much a &quot;latinization&quot; of the names, but rather which language was more important at each time, from italian to french to english, sometimes even to german.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-02T03:42:02-07:00","id":1488783,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gurkhal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487755-divorcing-clans-from-geography-people?p=1488767#post1488767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I have to disagree somewhat. By using Latin names, yes, we can push the origin of the names back one or two thousand years or so, but it don't make them the original names that the Clans would have used in their early history.<br /> <br /> EDITED: Besides I don't get the feeling that the Roman Empire was such a huge thing for the Cainites that it would have left a strong legacy like that.<br /> <br /> Secondly I would think that there would have developed certains terms used across mortal borders within the Kindred/Cainite subculture. Thus that there's a term of &quot;Lasombra&quot; for this Clan that has grown to become commonly used even while there may be local terms for local use as well. A Ventrue might use the term of Princeps, but for ease of commuication (s)he should also be familiar with the internationally accepted term &quot;Ventrue&quot; for her/his Clan..</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh no, I wasnt intending of naming the clans in the ancient fictional language of Ennoquian, nor in the also fictional &quot;language of the angels&quot; Fabulare that would've been used by Adam and Eve in the Garden of Heaven or before the Babel Tower. And, if we wanted to go further back in time, we could use names in babylonian, sumerian and egyptian. The thing is thou, the idea was to have then clans adapt to the local cultures. The original names would be absolutely lost in time, and it has always bothered me to have a somewhat alien name such as &quot;Ventrue&quot; which is just a collection of random letters just mixed togheter to sound cool, but that doesnt mean anything in any language, so it's an indication that it could've been the original name - in ancient &quot;ennoquian&quot; probably - while at the same time also having &quot;Brujah&quot; and &quot;Lasombra&quot;, respectivelly &quot;Witch&quot; and &quot;Theshadown&quot; in Spanish, who is a fairly recent language who's modern incarnation is no more than 300 years old, thus fairly recent in terms of cainite history, and also with some french-like (because it's not real french, it's just to sound like) name as &quot;Toreador&quot; or the english-like &quot;Malkavian&quot;, just names that sound like very modern languages; I mean, none of those clans would even call themselves that when the Camarilla was formed, at the time ALL of the european languages were vastly different from their modern forms - I for example cant understand 16th century &quot;portuguese&quot; AT ALL. It's a completely different language from the portuguese we speak today.<br /> <br /> Latin on the other hand is language that remained unchanged and that was vastly used in Europe throghout the centuries, particularly by the aristocracy - and lets remember, vampires are always people of note. So, the adoption of latim by the cainites, even as a frank (common) language not only between nations but also between generations, would not be too of a stretch. And, you would have to be REALLY ancient - and hidden behind a rock - to not be familiar with latin if you lived in western Europe. Only vampires older than 2.500 years - and who remained in torpor for at least 2.000 of those years - would not be familiar with latin. So it's an extremely unlikely proposition.<br /> <br /> And to say that latin wasnt important for western vampires would be just absurd. No language would be as important to cainites in western europe. I bet every western elder would be able to speak latin even today - in fact, I would even go as far as to say that this could be a case where cainite culture influenced mortal culture, with the cultural significance of the latin language being preserved in Europe at least in part due to cainite influence.<br /> <br /> The same would happen for greek in eastern Europe, arab AND greek in north middle east but also farsi (persian) for south Asia and mandarin for southeast Asia, and Bantu and Arab (mostly) for Africa.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487755-divorcing-clans-from-geography-people?p=1488761#post1488761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">in other places and/or times the Clan names were/are different. For example, in Spanish speaking countries it\u2019s unlikely that Lasombra is called Lasombra, which would be like calling them Theshadow. </div> </div> </div> </div>In the cases of &quot;Brujah&quot; and &quot;Lasombra&quot;, respectfully &quot;Witch&quot; and &quot;Theshadow&quot; in Spanish, I could see those being used by MORTALS. A medieval superstitious mortal shitting on his pants sees some &quot;demon&quot; in human form doing clearly supernatural stuff, he calls that &quot;demon&quot; as a &quot;witch&quot; (literally, Brujah). Or, that other type of &quot;demonic force&quot; lurking in the shadows, the spaniard mortal calls &quot;Lasombra&quot; (literally &quot;TheShadow&quot;).<br /> (And a week later, the cainites responsible for those superstitious suffer a blood hunt).<br /> <br /> Therefore, I find it unlikely that the &quot;Brujah&quot; would EVER call themselves as Brujah, anywhere, any time. Unless we are seriously considering that a vampiric clan would ever refer to themselves as &quot;Witches&quot;.<br /> <br /> Just imagine this, during the height of the Inquisition, vampires calling each other as witches in the most important language at the time.<br /> <br /> &quot;So Gusm\u00e1n, have you assembled &quot;the witches&quot; yet?&quot;<br /> &quot;No my lord Esteban, &quot;the Shadows&quot; have been causing trouble lately, so I was unable to do it&quot;<br /> <br /> Yeah, right.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24689,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","user":"Kakost","date":". 08-02-2022, 07:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-02T05:46:24-07:00","id":1488807,"title":"","content":"I mean I guess it's plausible that the Brujah, as rebels, and perhaps as a display of bravado, could have chosen to appropriate the word Brujah for themselves as a way of giving the finger to the Catholic Inquisition. &quot;We're <i>so</i> not scared of the Inquisition that's targeting both witches and vampires, that we vampires are going to double down by calling ourselves witches.&quot;<br /> <br /> The reality though is that the Clans were named in the early 90s by some white dudes who didn't really know all that much about the world and sometimes just picked names because they thought they were cool. Hell, Clan Giovanni was named after <span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#202122\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Rein-Hagen's favorite Italian restaurant (Giovanni's which got its name from the owner's first name) - which is why the Clan doesn't follow Italian naming conventions. The creators didn't know enough Italian to realize that Giovanni is a first name, not a last name (it would be like if they had Clan Steve, which wouldn't work. Steve is a first name, not a last name. Something like Stephenson could work, but Steve on its own wouldn't be representative of an English last name in the same way Giovanni is not representative of Italian last names).</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">We're sort of forced to look back and come up with in-setting reasons or excuses as to why the Clans and other groups have weird naming conventions because those are the official names. So even if they don't necessarily make sense by our reasoning they must make sense in-setting somehow.</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-02T06:19:02-07:00","id":1488812,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487755-divorcing-clans-from-geography-people?p=1488807#post1488807\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean I guess it's plausible that the Brujah, as rebels, and perhaps as a display of bravado, could have chosen to appropriate the word Brujah for themselves as a way of giving the finger to the Catholic Inquisition. &amp;quot;We're <i>so</i> not scared of the Inquisition that's targeting both witches and vampires, that we vampires are going to double down by calling ourselves witches.&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> The reality though is that the Clans were named in the early 90s by some white dudes who didn't really know all that much about the world and sometimes just picked names because they thought they were cool. Hell, Clan Giovanni was named after <span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#202122\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Rein-Hagen's favorite Italian restaurant (Giovanni's which got its name from the owner's first name) - which is why the Clan doesn't follow Italian naming conventions. The creators didn't know enough Italian to realize that Giovanni is a first name, not a last name (it would be like if they had Clan Steve, which wouldn't work. Steve is a first name, not a last name. Something like Stephenson could work, but Steve on its own wouldn't be representative of an English last name in the same way Giovanni is not representative of Italian last names).</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">We're sort of forced to look back and come up with in-setting reasons or excuses as to why the Clans and other groups have weird naming conventions because those are the official names. So even if they don't necessarily make sense by our reasoning they must make sense in-setting somehow.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, absolutely. I fully understand that the entirety of the VtM was a work that has been a crescent. Cool but crude initial ideas, upon which more stuff have been pilling up over the years. And yes, absolutely, the original names were just simply stuff that sounded cool.<br /> <br /> But that's exactly what we are discussing here, a sort of alternate VtM, that would polish a few corners, with slight different clans and clans more adapted for an improved setting.<br /> <br /> The &quot;issue&quot; (not really an issue, just something that I think would be interesting to consider) with names would be to make this look more natural, instead of some randomly funny sounding things like &quot;Samedi&quot; or &quot;Tzimisce&quot;, and also having some actual background to those; for instance, while some of the latin names are still funny sounding words, they still have a root and some purpose on them. And lets be honest, the &quot;Princeps&quot; is far cooler than &quot;Ventrue&quot;, particularly because it is the root of the word &quot;Prince&quot;. I believe this is the best example, but the others can be thinkered with, I just choose a few examples. Another example: the Assamites in Western Europe could be &quot;Sicarius&quot; or &quot;Sicarii&quot; (assassin/assassins) or &quot;Carnifex&quot; (executioner, but also butcher) or &quot;Iudex/Iudice&quot; (judge/judges). All of those would be cool. I particularly liked &quot;Sicarius&quot;. Meanwhile, in Eastern Europe they could use the greek &quot;Dimios&quot; (assassins), in middle east they could be called &quot;Jalaad&quot; (arab for executioner), in chinese &quot;Guizichou&quot; and japanese &quot;Jajji&quot; (judge), and all of those still sound as cool funny names to us as &quot;Assamites&quot; nonetheless, and yet still represent the same vampiric families, just with different names. So, a Sicarius may not even know that a Jalaad is a brother, but they'll share the same properties of the blood nevertheless.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-02T07:22:11-07:00","id":1488817,"title":"","content":"Hard no to that. Ventrue is just so phonetically pleasing, it's bold and sounds halfway between two english words that are very fitting for the clan. Princeps is... aggressively lame. Like they're some Grammar school geeks. They're the most hard-social charismatic clan in the fucking game. Like they represent everything common people hate, and they're still so godamn fucking likeable in person. Of course their name should be calibrated for maximum dopeness.<br /> <br /> (Baron Samedi is a mythological thing too, the whole clan is tied to the figure you should do a little research before making statements like that. )<br /> Tzmisce works pretty well. Not knowing how to pronounce the name? For a clan with Vicissitude, that's a feature. Granted, this works with non phonetic languages like English only<br /> <br /> <br /> Yeah, a fair few clans have stupid names that just sound cool. But many of them are cool sounding without issues, or even clever roots.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 08-03-2022, 01:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-02T08:22:10-07:00","id":1488824,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487755-divorcing-clans-from-geography-people?p=1488783#post1488783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh no, I wasnt intending of naming the clans in the ancient fictional language of Ennoquian, nor in the also fictional &quot;language of the angels&quot; Fabulare that would've been used by Adam and Eve in the Garden of Heaven or before the Babel Tower. And, if we wanted to go further back in time, we could use names in babylonian, sumerian and egyptian.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wasn't saying that fictional languages should be used, although their use would avoid the problem of trampling on the toes of real people in real cultures. So that's something to consider given how Cainites are also fictional.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487755-divorcing-clans-from-geography-people?p=1488783#post1488783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing is thou, the idea was to have then clans adapt to the local cultures. The original names would be absolutely lost in time, and it has always bothered me to have a somewhat alien name such as &quot;Ventrue&quot; which is just a collection of random letters just mixed togheter to sound cool, but that doesnt mean anything in any language, so it's an indication that it could've been the original name - in ancient &quot;ennoquian&quot; probably - while at the same time also having &quot;Brujah&quot; and &quot;Lasombra&quot;, respectivelly &quot;Witch&quot; and &quot;Theshadown&quot; in Spanish, who is a fairly recent language who's modern incarnation is no more than 300 years old, thus fairly recent in terms of cainite history, and also with some french-like (because it's not real french, it's just to sound like) name as &quot;Toreador&quot; or the english-like &quot;Malkavian&quot;, just names that sound like very modern languages; I mean, none of those clans would even call themselves that when the Camarilla was formed, at the time ALL of the european languages were vastly different from their modern forms - I for example cant understand 16th century &quot;portuguese&quot; AT ALL. It's a completely different language from the portuguese we speak today.</div> </div> </div> </div>To start with, Latin might work well for former High Clans but given how most people in Europe didn't know Latin at all so I find it odd that they would have only Latin names for Clans not heavily connected with the upper classes. Thus we would need at least two names. One in Latin for the upper class Cainites and then also local names in the common language of the majority of people.<br /> <br /> I'm sorry to your you couldn't read older texts in your language. I've read a fair bit of old texts when I was at uni and it was always the handwriting that gave my problems, not understanding what the words were, althought that also did happen.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487755-divorcing-clans-from-geography-people?p=1488783#post1488783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Latin on the other hand is language that remained unchanged and that was vastly used in Europe throghout the centuries, particularly by the aristocracy - and lets remember, vampires are always people of note. So, the adoption of latim by the cainites, even as a frank (common) language not only between nations but also between generations, would not be too of a stretch. And, you would have to be REALLY ancient - and hidden behind a rock - to not be familiar with latin if you lived in western Europe. Only vampires older than 2.500 years - and who remained in torpor for at least 2.000 of those years - would not be familiar with latin. So it's an extremely unlikely proposition.</div> </div> </div> </div>To the first part of vampire always being people of note I say: What!? Of note to their Sires, sure, but most Cainites would not come from the nobility in particular with the declining power and influence of said nobility over the centuries. There are several Clans, like Gangrel and Nosferatu, who seem pretty happy to Embrace people outside of the nobility.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487755-divorcing-clans-from-geography-people?p=1488783#post1488783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And to say that latin wasnt important for western vampires would be just absurd. No language would be as important to cainites in western europe. I bet every western elder would be able to speak latin even today - in fact, I would even go as far as to say that this could be a case where cainite culture influenced mortal culture, with the cultural significance of the latin language being preserved in Europe at least in part due to cainite influence.</div> </div> </div> </div>Most Elders would probably know, Latin, yes. As for their influence on human culture and society I am more sceptical.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-02T09:58:40-07:00","id":1488844,"title":"","content":"Just popping in to add the origin of the Ventrue clan name. As i feel it's something i can contribute to as a native french speaker.<br /> <br /> I have no official source, but i've read somewhere that Ventrue, was inspired by the French word ''Ventru'', which is an old french word. Ventru is an adjective that means ''to have a big belly''. The adjective most likely come from the word ''ventre''; the french word for belly.<br /> <br /> I personally think it's kinda fitting for the Ventrue. I know not much is know about the Ventrue Antediluvian, but given that most Antediluvian got a curse beffiting their vice, they might have been very gluttonous, which would explain the nature of the Ventrue's curse.<br /> <br /> Anyway, interesting thread, keep it up, it's a fun read. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Edit: After translating the word ''Ventru'' on google, the literal translation it gives is '' Potbellied''. ''Ventrue'' is also the feminine form of ''Ventru'' meaning it would be an adjective used to describe a female subject. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26771,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26771-algarik","user":"Algarik","date":".  To add a bit of context and precision. 08-02-2022, 01:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26771-algarik","name":"Algarik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26771_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"115"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-02T11:10:09-07:00","id":1488857,"title":"","content":"I think it's best to just accept that the official names and many game terms are an artifact of it being an RPG. The writers could either ransack obsolete or foreign words to come up with something that sounds &quot;real&quot; and evocative, or make up nonsense words that would likely sound false to people's ears. The actual terms use in the setting might be different, but don't worry about it. Verisimilitude can only go so far.<br /> <br /> The other thing I tell players in my chronicles is that each of the clans have had many names in different times and cultures. Obviously none of the clans were known by their corebook names during the times of Sargon of Akkad, Cyrus the Great, Julius Caesar, and so on. Likewise even now we have different clan names today if you want to go by certain geographical sourcebooks. The current names as we know them from the corebook is just from an &quot;official&quot; standardization of terms used by the Camarilla for the purposes of instructions to the Justicars and their use in Conclaves and such sometime around the 1600s or 1700s. They were probably chosen as some were popular nicknames at the time much like &quot;kooks&quot;, &quot;blue bloods&quot;, &quot;sewer rats&quot;, etc. are used today. That was just to provide clarity so people wouldn't argue that someone wasn't addressing the entire clan, but only a particular lineage or clan members in one particular part of the world. But the terms became popular and are used mainly exclusively today. The variety of older terms are still known, but mostly not used except by the elders in private conversations, when someone from a certain geographical region wants to make a point on how they are different from other members of their clan elsewhere, or perhaps by some Toreador when they really want to be poetic.<br /> <br /> I sometimes scribble down alternate names in my notes in case I ever want elders to speak in ways that showcase the difference in age between them and the PCs. Having Critias use a different name for his clan than the Brujah PC does helps gets the point across this a man from a different time despite his ability to fit in the contemporary world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-02T19:02:34-07:00","id":1488914,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gurkhal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487755-divorcing-clans-from-geography-people?p=1488824#post1488824\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To start with, Latin might work well for former High Clans but given how most people in Europe didn't know Latin at all so I find it odd that they would have only Latin names for Clans not heavily connected with the upper classes. Thus we would need at least two names. One in Latin for the upper class Cainites and then also local names in the common language of the majority of people.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not necessarily.<br /> <br /> While I'm not sold on changing their names, either, the idea that Latin names would have raised in prominence does make sense.<br /> <br /> Most people weren't literate in Latin and couldn't really speak it. But that doesn't mean they had no familiarity with it and couldn't learn a bunch of names, they definitely could and did. Indeed, for most of the Middle Ages most people in Europe would hear Latin spoken at least once a week during Mass, and almost every Roman Catholic in the world kept hearing it at Mass until 1965.<br /> <br /> It was not just a language of nobility. It was the language of erudition because it was the <i>Lingua Franca</i> of Europe, in a time when books took so much work to copy that translating was a waste, better to do it in Latin so you can pass on without worrying about the language of the receiver (individual books circled the world a lot back then).<br /> <br /> So a Latin name would be extremely useful as even if its meaning in the actual context of the language would be unknown for most, the name itself would be easy to recognize across Europe, and the spelling would be easier to understand even if with some accent.<br /> <br /> Also, we don't know how many people really spoke Latin back then, because while they could be illiterate in it, speaking it would still be very useful. People traveled as much or maybe more than they travel today, and many, maybe most, would do a pilgrimage at least once in their lives, which meant a long journey through many countries. Between the personal need to have a common language when asking directions and the mere exposure to foreign travelers using it, it is well within the realm of possibility that Latin was still widely spoken, even if in a broken, patchwork way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}